{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T17:43:51.036Z","ordinal":7692,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9","turn_id":"01a0ba4f-3944-7ce3-88ac-4c7975e84b1b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f4897f73-ba82-40d2-854c-9358f2e14798","process_id":"22294","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib,json,shutil\nb=pathlib.Path('/Users/thomi/.codex/visualizations/2026/09/18/01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9/code-quality-audit');p=b/'coverage.json';a=json.loads(p.read_text())\nfor x in a:\n if x['path']=='docs/reference.md':x.update(review_status='source-inspected',checks=['Complete 1357-line document read; local Markdown link resolution across all repository Markdown.'],notes='F101 ten broken relative links. Excessive repeated installation narrative and stale references to itself as README.')\np.write_text(json.dumps(a,indent=2)+'\\n');shutil.copyfile('/tmp/audit-doc-links.py',b/'evidence/audit-doc-links.py')\nwith (b/'expanded-findings.md').open('a') as f:f.write('''\\n## F101 — P3: Reference guide has ten broken local links\\nLocation: `docs/reference.md:79–82`, `240`, `815`, `1104`, `1264`, `1354–1357`. Links resolve relative to docs/reference.md but retain repo-root prefixes: docs/operations.md becomes docs/docs/operations.md, and benchmarks/agent-brain/... becomes docs/benchmarks/agent-brain/.... None exists. This breaks navigation from the primary reference to installation, MCP, privacy and benchmark contracts. Use sibling filenames for docs and ../benchmarks/... for benchmark references. Read-only Markdown scan found exactly ten missing local file targets across the repository; all ten are in this file. Evidence: evidence/audit-doc-links.py and audit-doc-links.json. No source-symbol relationship is involved.\\n\\nReference editorial notes: 1357-line document retains long repeated installation narrative and calls itself README. Says no-agent setup “installs nothing” although it builds 