{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T17:47:01.173Z","ordinal":7744,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_0cb48b2b18d09e75016aaeca92dcb887d28f366d258e8698dc","status":"completed","call_id":"call_4DPLQ0Al65rsslVjjJqEuwvp","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '305,331p' docs/semantic_mcp_guide.md; sed -n '1,42p' docs/recall_threat_model.md; cat docs/release-blockers.md docs/ga-readiness.md docs/eval_ledger.md\",\"max_output_tokens\":7000}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0ba4f-3944-7ce3-88ac-4c7975e84b1b","create_time":1789840014.379795}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T17:47:01.269Z","ordinal":7745,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9","turn_id":"01a0ba4f-3944-7ce3-88ac-4c7975e84b1b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8e29a37e-50d0-4e04-846d-904ea2d34066","process_id":"21011","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '305,331p' docs/semantic_mcp_guide.md; sed -n '1,42p' docs/recall_threat_model.md; cat docs/release-blockers.md docs/ga-readiness.md docs/eval_ledger.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '305,331p' docs/semantic_mcp_guide.md; sed -n '1,42p' docs/recall_threat_model.md; cat docs/release-blockers.md docs/ga-readiness.md docs/eval_ledger.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"\n- `brain_delete_project` accepts only the bound repo's key. A foreign `repo_key`\n  is refused; the deletion is irreversible and `confirm=true` is no protection\n  against a prompt-injected agent that supplies it itself.\n- `brain_list_projects` returns only the bound project, not every locally\n  indexed repo's key, brain path, and index counts.\n- `brain_workspace_graph`, `brain_workspace_regressions`, and\n  `brain_workspace_review` refuse a workspace the bound repository is not a\n  member of, or one whose repos live outside the bound repository's parent\n  directory. Sibling checkouts under a common parent — `devenv/cli` alongside\n  `devenv/entiredb`, the layout `entire brain workspace add` produces — are in\n  scope without the opt-in.\n\nAn unbound server refuses project listing, deletion, and workspace tools by\ndefault. Workspace keys must match their local checkouts, and execution uses\nthe same manifest snapshot that passed the scope checks.\n\nSet `ENTIRE_BRAIN_MCP_ALLOW_CROSS_REPO=1` on the server to opt back into\ncross-repo behaviour (the sibling of `ENTIRE_BRAIN_MCP_ALLOW_ANY_PATH`, which\ndoes the same for `brain_index_repository`'s path argument). The refusal message\nalways names the variable. None of this touches the `entire brain ...` CLI: a\nhuman at a terminal keeps every cross-repo verb, gate unset.\n\n`brain_patterns` and `brain_patterns_status` are read-only pattern-corpus\ninspection tools. Skill formation is intentionally not exposed as an MCP write\ntool; use the explicit CLI flow `entire brain patterns skills form` when a human\nor authorized automation wants to synthesize a skill.\n# Recall threat model: prompt injection and secret retention\n\nScope: the conversational-memory and history recall surfaces (CLI retrieval\nverbs, MCP tools, brief, bundles/publish, logs, and the derived stores), per\nPhase 4 deliverable 7 of the conversational-memory plan. This documents what\nthe code enforces today, where the boundaries are, and the residual risks with\ntheir tracking state. It is a living document: change the code, change this.\n\n## Assets\n\n- **Captured transcripts** (exported copies under the brain's `sessions/`):\n  may contain secrets typed or pasted during sessions, hostile text copied\n  from the web or from repo content, and instruction-like text of any origin.\n- **Derived projections**: history index (classic records + conversation\n  exchange projections), FTS stores, vector stores, scan caches, pattern\n  episodes/corpus, durable facts, distill caches.\n- **Published artifacts**: brain bundles (semantic snapshots, overlays, facts).\n- **Receipts and logs**: serve receipts, watch output, MCP debug log.\n\n## Adversary channels and enforced boundaries\n\n### 1. Hostile content inside recalled history (prompt injection at recall)\n\nRecalled conversation text is attacker-influencable by construction: anything\na past session read (web pages, repo files, tool output) can plant\ninstruction-like text that later surfaces in retrieval.\n\nEnforced:\n\n- Every conversation result carries `verification_required: true` plus a\n  machine-readable `historical_conversation` caveat on every surface (CLI\n  JSON, MCP JSON, text rendering) stating recalled content is quoted data,\n  never instructions. The canary test proves an instruction-like string is\n  returned only inside this wrapper.\n- Tool and skill descriptions never instruct an agent to obey recalled\n  content; the recall skill's safety contract is test-locked\n  (`TestRecallSkillTemplatesEmbeddedAndSafe`).\n- Hidden reasoning, raw tool output, and injected wrapper/pseudo-user\n  messages are excluded from exchange text at extraction; harness noise (API\n  error envelopes, hook injections) is filtered.\n- `matched_terms` explainability exposes why weak matches surfaced, so\n  low-signal bait is diagnosable.\n# Release Blockers\n\nA register of release-gating findings from the PR #33 review (2026-06-11),\nkept next to the audit so a release decision can see what is open, what was\nfixed, and exactly why. The standard for this file is the eval ledger's:\nexplicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\n\n## RESOLVED AS CLAIM DEMOTION — B1: Answer-bearing query hints invalidated the old replay-lab proof\n\n**The claim under audit.** `docs/release_readiness_audit.md` previously treated\nthree replay-lab suites as citable proof that history/MCP/Radar context improved\nagent outcomes without handing over hidden validation or expected text. That\nattribution was unsupported.\n\n**The confound.** `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py` injects `brain_queries` into\nbrain/MCP-arm prompts only; the `no_brain` arm receives none. In the retained\npre-B1 suites, several `brain_queries` contained answer-bearing identifiers,\nhidden-test names, or near-verbatim hidden-validation strings. The old\ncomparison therefore measured *(answer-bearing hint + brain)* versus *(no hint,\nno brain)*, not brain value alone.\n\n**Fixes landed.**\n\n- `brain_query_leak_audit` now rejects answer-bearing `brain_queries` before a\n  panel can run. It checks code-shaped identifiers and verbatim 3+-word phrases\n  against hidden fix text and paths, expected files, hidden validation commands,\n  expected-string greps, hidden test names, and validation fixture contents.\n- All committed benchmark task queries that tripped the auditor were rewritten\n  to symptom-level retrieval terms. The all-task sweep now reports zero flagged\n  task files.\n- The retained evidence manifest is stricter again: even in `no_release_claim`\n  mode it requires zero hard integrity flags.\n- The old confounded retained suites were removed from\n  `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release` and replaced with clean reruns.\n\n**Clean rerun result (2026-06-11).** Item 3 is now complete: the three promoted\nsuites were rerun from a clean checkout with the sanitized task configs, four\nrepetitions per side, retained panel provenance, and host paths redacted before\ncommit. The independent audit now reports 3 suites, 24 records, 24/24 provenance\ncomplete, 0 hard integrity flags, 8 MCP-verified datapoints, 4 completed\nnamed-tool Radar datapoints, and 0 proof-ready comparisons.\n\n| Clean retained suite | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `release-candidate-entire-brain-schema-contract-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but noisy: pass rate 50% -> 75%, mean score 86.5 -> 87.75, `proof_ready=false`. |\n| `release-candidate-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.25 -> 91.25, `proof_ready=false`. |\n| `release-candidate-cli-radar-mcp-del-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.5 -> 90.5, `proof_ready=false`. |\n\n**Current release implication.** B1 is resolved as an integrity/confound blocker:\nthe retained release lane no longer contains answer-bearing query-hint artifacts.\nIt is still `no_release_claim`, because the clean reruns did not produce a\nproof-ready replay-lab lift. Any future agent-lift claim needs harder clean\nretained tasks that survive the proof-ready gate; the old numbers stay removed\nfrom the release story.\n\nOperationalization note: the literal \"any token\" wording from the review is not\nimplemented because it would false-flag ordinary symptom text. The enforced rule\nis code-shaped identifiers plus verbatim 3+-word phrases, with the known residual\nthat 1-2 word plain-English overlaps are not flagged.\n\n## RESOLVED — fixed during review on this branch\n\n**R1 — Eval label discipline orphaned the history-eval pipeline** (fixed in\n`15e7aaa`). `validateEvalTask` rejected `history-eval-gen` output and every\nretained task file; `eval-compare` hard-errored on its own default eval-gen\noutput. Fix separates ground-*truth* (same explicit labels, same source →\ncomparable) from evidence *grade* (human/judge-refined → claimable);\nhistory-eval now declares `provenance_silver`, legacy files default to it,\nand side-dependent truths (`source_match`, runtime judge) stay gated behind\n`--allow-proxy-comparison`. Covered by a new gen→load→run→compare seam test.\n\n**R2 — Retrieval panic on the loopback guard's own rejection path** (fixed in\n`15e7aaa`). `configuredEmbedder` dereferenced the nil returned for a\nnon-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBED_URL`; every `search`/`vsearch`/`query`\ncrashed in the exact scenario the guard hardens. Now degrades to the bundled\nModel2Vec embedder with a warning; regression test added.\n\n**R3 — Brain write-lock scoping** (fixed in `15e7aaa`). Export held the\nexclusive lock across the minutes-long transcript phase while every other\nuser times out at 10s — failing a concurrent distill's FINAL flush (an\nhours-long run killed at its last step) — and `openHistoryFTS` took the write\nlock on the query READ path, serializing all searches. Export now locks only\nthe shared-artifact phases; FTS opens fresh indexes lock-free and\ndouble-checks freshness under the lock only for rebuilds.\n\n**R4 — Silent full re-distill on upgrade** (fixed alongside this file). The\nfingerprint salt plus the stable-branch-dir rename invalidated every existing\ncache entry, and the shipped \"legacy key\" fallback could never match (a\nlegacy-format fingerprint never equals a salted one) — the first post-upgrade\nrun would re-distill the entire corpus (observed scale: ~14h of agent calls\nfor a 2,640-session brain). Fixed with lazy grandfathering: the legacy\nformula is kept genuinely computable (including pre-rename transcript paths),\na matching legacy entry counts as cached and is rewritten under the new\nkey/format on first touch, and the transcript path is no longer hashed into\nthe new fingerprint at all — storage layout is not identity, and hashing it\nre-invalidates the world on every future layout change. The filtered-session\ncarry-through, which copied legacy-format fingerprints under new-format keys\n(making them permanently unmatchable), now preserves entries under their own\nkeys. Covered by `TestDistillCacheGrandfathersLegacyEntries`, including the\nrenamed-branch-dir case and the changed-content negative.\n# P0 GA readiness — entire-graph + entire-brain + GraphMark\n\nA single, cross-repo checklist for the P0 General Availability of the local brain:\nthe semantic provider (`entire-graph`), the brain (`entire-brain`), and the eval\nharness (`GraphMark`). The standard here matches `docs/release-blockers.md` and\n`docs/release_readiness_audit.md`: explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\n\n## GA gate — everything below must hold on one aligned release SHA\n\n| # | Gate | State | Evidence |\n|---|------|-------|----------|\n| 1 | `entire-graph` module path is the org namespace | ✅ done | `go.mod` = `github.com/entireio/entire-graph` (migrated) |\n| 2 | `entire-graph` version stamped from a real tag | ✅ done | tag `v0.1.0`; `scripts/release.sh` injects `-X main.version=$(git describe --tags)` |\n| 3 | Provider schema is a frozen, pinnable GA contract | ✅ done | ADR 0001 — schema `1.x` (minor `1.1`), additive-only, tolerant readers |\n| 4 | Brain pins the provider at the live repo | ✅ done | `entire-plugin.yml` `repo_url` → `github.com/entireio/entire-graph` |\n| 5 | No-egress + deterministic golden coverage | ✅ exists | `doctor` `no_egress:true`; golden/provider/quality tests green (GA acceptance bar) |\n| 6 | `brain_*` MCP tool contract locked | ✅ exists | schemas `additionalProperties:false`, unknown-key rejection, named-tool auditability |\n| 7 | GraphMark wired as a regression gate | ✅ done | `GraphMark` CI: self-tests + significance no-drift; floor = 28/30 languages, 1148 vs 802 |\n| 8 | Phase-1 local-only boundary frozen as a guardrail | ✅ exists | stdio MCP only; `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` / `LOCAL_ONLY` documented |\n| 9 | Release blockers B1 + R1–R4 confirmed closed on RC SHA | ✅ done | `mise run release:evidence` on the RC SHA: 0 hard integrity flags, 24/24 records with required provenance. See \"GA cut — resolved\" §1 and `docs/release-blockers.md` |\n| 10 | Tagged `main` on `entire-graph` **and** `entire-brain`, aligned | ✅ done | both cut `v0.1.0` on the aligned GA SHA. See \"GA cut — resolved\" §2 and \"Provider compatibility since the GA cut\" below |\n| 11 | `no_release_claim` items resolved (proof or scoped-out) | ✅ resolved | see \"Claim posture\" below |\n\n## Compatibility matrix\n\n| Producer | Contract | Consumer | Rule |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `entire-graph` schema | `1.x` (ADR 0001) | `entire-brain` ingestion | accept any `1.x`, ignore unknown fields, warn on newer minor |\n| `entire-graph` provider | `provider_version` in manifest header | `entire-brain` refresh | recorded, not gated; used for provenance |\n| `GraphMark` harness | committed `*.score.json` + `stats_significance.py` | CI regression gate | significance report must regenerate byte-identical; corpus/harness changes must re-commit it |\n\nPinning guidance: brain consumers may pin the provider `>=1.0 <2.0`; a `2.0` is a\nbreaking change with a migration note and is out of the P0 `1.x` line.\n\n## Claim posture (honest — never overclaimed)\n\n- **Semantic usefulness — CLAIMABLE.** Backed by `GraphMark`: Entire beats the\n  comparison baseline on **28 of 30 top languages** at exact-McNemar p<0.05\n  (C# p=0.07 and PHP p=0.18 lead on rate but sit just under significance — more\n  scored repos, not a loss), overall **1,148 vs 802** correct (91% vs 64%,\n  p≈0), with Benjamini-Hochberg multiple-comparisons control. This is the first\n  broad, reproducible, in-repo-gated proof and supersedes the earlier single\n  narrow condition-level result.\n- **Distill wall-clock (>24h target-repo timing) — NO CLAIM.** Only ~2× local\n  proof (`audit_distill_perf.py`) exists; the >24h target-repo evidence was never\n  collected. GA makes **no distill-speed claim**; scoped out until measured.\n- **Durable-facts-vs-raw — NO CLAIM.** The four-arm harness exists but there are\n  **zero active durable facts**, so there is no paired proof. Facts ship as a\n  capability with **no comparative-quality claim** until seeded facts + paired\n  evidence land.\n\nThese match `docs/release_readiness_audit.md`; nothing here is asserted beyond its\nevidence.\n\n## Distribution\n\n- **P0 channel: signed release archives.** `entire-graph/scripts/release.sh` emits\n  per-OS/arch tarballs under `dist/` with `SHA256SUMS`; that is the GA artifact.\n  Install is via the Entire CLI plugin flow pinned at the tagged release.\n- **Marketplace / plugin-discovery listing: out of scope for P0**, tracked as a\n  post-GA follow-up.\n\n## GA cut — resolved\n\n1. ✅ **Release evidence gate passed.** `mise run release:evidence` on the RC SHA:\n   **0 hard integrity flags**, 24/24 records with required provenance (source\n   base/head + harness/config/tool hashes). B1 + R1–R4 hold.\n2. ✅ **Both repos tagged, aligned.** `entire-graph` `v0.1.0` and `entire-brain`\n   `v0.1.0` cut on the aligned GA SHA.\n3. ✅ **MCP surfaces verified independent** (no longer referenced-not-verified):\n   the brain stdio server (`entire brain mcp`, 34 `brain_*` tools) and the CLI's\n   hidden `entire mcp` (2 tools: `agent_help`, `entire_status`) are two separate\n   binaries with **disjoint tool namespaces, distinct `serverInfo`, no proxy, no\n   collision**. Decision: **intentionally separate** — brain owns the rich\n   memory/graph surface, the CLI owns a thin status/help surface for MCP-host\n   agents without a hook channel. The only divergences (framing: brain dual /\n   CLI NDJSON-only; fallback protocol `2024-11-05` vs `2025-06-18`; max frame\n   4 MiB vs 1 MiB) are cosmetic, cause no current-state breakage, and are\n   deferred to the P2 unified-MCP-surface work — not a P0 blocker.\n\n## Provider compatibility since the GA cut\n\nGate 10 pinned the aligned `v0.1.0` ↔ `v0.1.0` GA cut. `entire-graph` has since\nreleased `v0.2.0` (2026-07-16) and `v0.3.0` (2026-08-14) while `entire-brain`\nremains at `v0.1.0`. The tags are no longer numerically aligned; the **contract**\nstill is, and that is what gate 10 protects:\n\n- `entire-graph` `v0.3.0` still advertises `SchemaVersion = \"1.1\"`\n  (`internal/sem/provider.go`) — the same version cut at GA, and within the\n  additive-only `1.x` major that ADR 0001 freezes.\n- The emitted `record_type` set is unchanged: `file`, `symbol`, `relation`,\n  `external`, `summary` — all of which the brain's snapshot reader already\n  handles.\n- The brain consumes `entire graph snapshot` and `entire graph doctor` only. It\n  does not call `entire graph search`, so search-path work (multi-resolution\n  prose retrieval, `--single-resolution` / `--document-resolution`) does not\n  reach the brain's ingestion path.\n\nNo brain-side adaptation is required to run against `entire-graph` `v0.3.0`.\nRe-check this section on any `entire-graph` **major** bump, which by ADR 0001 is\nthe only release permitted to break the reader.\n\n**P0 GA status: gates 1–11 satisfied.** The local brain (entire-graph + entire-brain\n+ GraphMark) is at GA on the `v0.1.0` line.\n# Eval ledger\n\n> Naming note: recorded `search` and `vsearch` commands remain compatibility\n> aliases. Current usage is `query --keyword` and `query --semantic`; plain\n> `query` remains hybrid. Historical results below retain their original names.\n\nOne row per retrieval-quality or agent-outcome measurement that gated a decision. The task sets,\ncorpus snapshots, and metrics differ between rows — **numbers are comparable\nonly within a row's own baseline**, never across rows. Before claiming a\nregression or a win, find the row whose gate you are re-testing and reproduce\nits exact config; the source doc has the repro commands.\n\n| Date | Corpus / tasks | Comparison | Headline | Decision it gated | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-06-08 | entire-brain `main`, 179 facts, 16 provenance-labeled tasks (`facts eval-gen`, k=10) | lexical-only vs Model2Vec fused | lexical 0.86 → fused **1.50 useful/1k** (+76%); concept stratum 0 → 0.79 | Frozen Stage 0 baseline; any later embedder swap must beat 1.50 on this set. Also: facts FTS5 BM25 measured at parity (1.43), so BM25 ships **opt-in** (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_FACTS_BM25=1`), not default | `../alignment.md` (Stage 0); artifacts at `<brain>/eval/baseline-20260608/` |\n| 2026-06-08 | same 16-task set | Model2Vec fused vs EmbeddingGemma-300M (Q8_0, shell-to-local-server runner) | **1.80 useful/1k (+20%)**, precision 0.106, concept stratum 1.68 (2.1×); gain is reachability (three 0.00→~1.75 rescues), not uniform lift | Stage 1b embedder **quality gate: passed**. Runtime/distribution work still parked | `../alignment.md` (Stage 1b) |\n| 2026-06-08 | entire-brain (16 tasks) + podcasts (44 tasks), pooled n=60 | Model2Vec vs EmbeddingGemma, second repo | pooled 1.77 → **2.00 useful/1k (+14%)**; +13% on the non-meta repo | Confirms the Gemma gain is not a meta-domain artifact; right-sizes the effect from +20% to a moderate +14% | `../alignment.md` (multi-repo confirmation) |\n| 2026-06-08 | live 32k-record history index | substring scorer vs FTS5 BM25 (history) | `matches: null` defect fixed: BM25's IDF replaces the 3-of-N term-coverage gate; Model2Vec on history measured as **noise** (negative cosine separation), EmbeddingGemma separates (0.397 > 0.317) | History ships **BM25-only by default** (Stage 1a); a history semantic arm waits for the Stage 1b embedder | `../alignment.md` (Stage 1a findings) |\n| 2026-06-09 | entire-brain `main`, 930 facts, 17 deterministic tasks | frozen B0 baseline | lexical 1.063 useful/1k, semantic 1.013 | Appendix D (B1–B4) work measured against this snapshot | `durable_facts_handover.md` (B0) |\n| 2026-06-09 | pooled n=118 (17 entire-brain + 101 entire-cli tasks) | flat vs locus-**scoped** vs outline retrieval arms | scoped: **+59% useful/1k** (p=0.027 raw; marginal under Holm), −112 tokens (p<0.001), recall −0.029 (p=0.004); outline not a retrieval win (p=0.51) | B4 verdict: **scoped retrieval validated**; outline kept as a human-readable map, not a ranking mechanism; scoped-floor variant killed | `durable_facts_handover.md` (B4) |\n| 2026-06-09 | 121-task benchmark (potion-retrieval-32M) | lexical vs Model2Vec fused (shipped config) | **+0.459 useful/1k** (p=0.005, Holm-significant), precision +0.025 (p=0.013), no token cost | Phase D ship decision: semantic fusion **default-on** for `recall`/`brief` | `durable_facts_handover.md` (Phase D) |\n| 2026-06-10 | entire-brain live brain, **history layer**: 33.8k rankable records, 13 provenance-labeled tasks (`history-eval-gen`, k=10) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused (`history-eval` arms) | substring 0.315 → **BM25 0.927 useful/1k (2.9×)**, precision 0.062 → 0.146 — first quantitative confirmation of the shipped BM25 default. Cutoff sweep 0.15/0.30/0.50: **within noise** → the shipped 0.30 stands. Fused (Model2Vec) 1.219 (+31% over BM25), 4W/3L/6T — **directional only**: n=13 with 6 all-zero tasks leaves 7 informative pairs, far from significant. Tension with the 2026-06-08 \"M2V noise on history\" probe is real but explainable: that probe measured raw cosine separation on paraphrases; RRF fusion bounds how much a weak semantic arm can hurt while letting its agreements help | History eval harness landed (`history-eval-gen` / `history-eval`); cutoff question **closed**; history semantic arm **stays unshipped** pending an EmbeddingGemma run (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBEDDER=ollama … --arm fused`) and a second repo | this repo (`internal/cli/history_eval.go`); task set regenerable via `history-eval-gen` |\n\n| 2026-06-10 | three repos, **history layer**: entire-brain (13 tasks), podcasts (16), entire-cli (**882**, 267k records) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused vs **EmbeddingGemma-fused** (canonical GGUF via node-llama-cpp server) | useful/1k — podcasts: 1.128 / 1.554 / 1.731 / **2.108**; entire-brain: 0.315 / 0.927 / 1.219 / 0.978; entire-cli: 0.283 / 1.016 / 1.033 / **1.158**. At n=882: M2V-fused is **parity** with BM25 (+1.7% — the small-repo +31% was noise, consistent with the original M2V-noise probe), while **Gemma-fused is +14% (329W/248L/305T, sign test p=0.00075)** — the same +14% the facts layer measured, now decision-grade on history | **History semantic arm: validated with EmbeddingGemma, not with Model2Vec.** Production wiring (fused history arm when a Gemma embedder is configured; history vectors in vec0) is now justified but not yet built. BM25 default reconfirmed at scale (3.6× substring) | this repo (`history-eval` fused arm); per-repo JSONs regenerable |\n\n| 2026-06-10 | entire-brain live brain, **midtask stratum**: 33 tasks (20 midtask) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused, per stratum | midtask useful/1k: 0.317 / 0.631 / 0.881 — BM25's lift over substring is **smaller on midtask (2.0×)** than on opening concept queries (5.9×), and fusion helps midtask most in relative terms (+40% over BM25). n=20, directional | Mid-session questions are a real, harder stratum; powered confirmation queued on the entire-cli v4 re-scan and the entire.io capstone | this repo (`history-eval-gen --midtask`) |\n| 2026-06-11 | entire-cli v4 index (273k records, 6.2k requests), **1,522 tasks** incl. **632 midtask** | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused, per stratum, paired | midtask useful/1k: 0.260 / 0.709 / 0.737. BM25 over substring holds on every stratum (2.7×–5.1×) but is **weakest on midtask (2.7×)**. M2V-fused vs BM25: **overall parity (453W/425L, p=0.34)** — consistent with the three-repo finding — but **positive on the midtask stratum (181W/144L, p=0.040)**: even the weak embedder helps where questions are narrow and in-flight | Item 8 premise confirmed at power: the midtask stratum leans on semantics where opening requests do not. Evaluate retrieval levers against it before shipping hook-path defaults; the Gemma midtask read rides the entire.io capstone batch | this repo (`history-eval-gen` v4) |\n| 2026-06-12 | **capstone**: entire.io v4 (**418k records, 2,584 tasks**, 1,049 midtask) + entire-cli v4 (1,522 tasks, 632 midtask), paired per-task t-tests | BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused vs **EmbeddingGemma-fused**, first read at production scale | entire.io useful/1k: BM25 0.883 / M2V 0.857 / **Gemma 0.998 (+13%, t=7.08)**; precision: Gemma **+0.016 (t=7.68)** while **M2V −0.013 (t=−6.33)** — at 418k records the weak embedder costs significant precision and buys nothing. entire-cli replicates: Gemma +12.5% useful/1k (t=5.09), precision +0.017 (t=6.38); M2V precision **−0.007 (t=−2.84)**, useful/1k parity (t=0.73). Midtask: Gemma beats BM25 on both repos (t=5.19 eio / t=2.06 cli); the 06-11 cli M2V midtask positive does **not** generalize — eio midtask M2V is flat (t=0.33). Third independent ~+13% Gemma read (facts +14%, three-repo history +14%, capstone +13%/+12.5%) | **Item 9 verdict: ship the history fused arm gated on a configured Gemma-class embedder; Model2Vec fusion on history is a closed negative at scale.** BM25 stays the no-embedder default. (Substring arm abandoned mid-run: its per-task re-scoring is O(tasks×records) — 6.5h without finishing at this scale; its baseline is already established at 2.7–5.1× on three repos) | this repo (`history-eval`); artifacts in `~/.entire-brain-eval/` (regenerable) |\n| 2026-06-18 | entire-brain `main`, replay-lab clean correctness task (`entire-brain-clean-default-fact-merge-confidence`, a decided default whose value lives only in retained history), n=4/side, `claude:sonnet:high` | no_brain vs full_brain (history channel), **end-to-end agent validation pass-rate** | no_brain **0/4** → full_brain **4/4**; `brain_positive_stable`, `proof_ready=true` (pass-rate lift surviving drop-one); `audit_codex.py` 0 hard integrity flags, 16/16 provenance-backed. no_brain cannot recover the exact decided value; full_brain reads it from history and restores it | **First proof-ready replay-lab agent-lift.** Flips the history-channel correctness scope from `no_release_claim` to claimable; MCP/Radar/codex-runner/efficiency scopes stay no-claim. Co-located contract-checkpoint comparison saturated (both 4/4) | `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/replay-lab-clean/` (manifest + codex-audit-report); panel `p01-clean-proof-claude`; gate `mise run clean-proof:evidence` |\n| 2026-08-07 | entire-brain live brain, **conversation-exchange layer** (1,006 exchanges after dedupe): 22-task exact/paraphrase/failed/decision pack (v6 ids) + 10-task held paraphrase stratum, EmbeddingGemma via ollama (Intel CPU), dev-only n | conversation BM25 (search) vs BM25+Gemma RRF fusion (query) vs semantic-only (vsearch) | exact pack: lexical R@1 0.864 / R@5 1.000 / MRR 0.932 vs fused **0.773 / 0.955 / 0.864**; fusion displaced two rank-1 exact hits and dropped one paraphrase from rank 1 to unranked; held paraphrase stratum: lexical 4/10, fused **5/10** (+1), vsearch 5/10 with different coverage. Small n, one corpus, one embedder; directional, not significant | **Conversation fusion ships DARK behind ENTIRE_BRAIN_CONVERSATION_FUSION; conversation `query` stays BM25-only by default** (same eligibility discipline as history fusion: an arm turns on via a validated ledger row, not by existing). vsearch stays available as explicit semantic-only. Reopen with better embedding text (projection mixes request+response; consider request-weighted) and/or a larger pack | dev packs + scorer in session scratchpad (private; corpus identity); store `history/embeddings/conversation-vectors.sqlite` |\n| 2026-08-08 | entire-brain live brain post-consolidation (76,238 records; exchanges incl. the prior day's sessions), same 22-task exact pack + 10-task paraphrase stratum, EmbeddingGemma via ollama, dev-only n | conversation BM25 vs BM25+Gemma RRF fusion with **request-weighted embeddings** (`reqw1`: request line + 512 B response head, versioned store id) | lexical R@1 0.818 / R@5 1.000 / MRR 0.909 vs fused-reqw1 **0.909 / 0.909 / 0.909**; reqw1 REVERSES the mixed-text scheme's R@1 loss (fused now +0.091 over lexical; was −0.091) and keeps +1 paraphrase (5/10 vs 4/10), but two exact queries drop out of the top-5 entirely. Note the aging pack: the lexical baseline itself moved (0.864→0.818 R@1) as new sessions about the same topics joined the corpus | **reqw1 ships as the embedding scheme** (better fused profile, vsearch unchanged), but the fusion flag STAYS DARK: two complete top-5 dropouts on exact queries is still a real displacement cost at n=22. Next reopen avenue: asymmetric fusion weight (down-weight the semantic list) or a higher semantic-only calibration bar, plus a regenerated larger pack | dev packs + scorer in session scratchpad; store id `ollama:embeddinggemma:reqw1` |\n| 2026-08-08 | Live capture-loop journeys (sanctioned): real Claude Code (haiku) and Codex CLI sessions in isolated scratch repos under real `entire` capture (0.6.3-nightly), gated behind ENTIRE_BRAIN_LIVE_E2E=1 | full chain per journey: capture -> checkpoint fold on user commit -> incremental export -> delta recall BEFORE consolidation -> consolidation -> search/get/outline/receipts | Claude Code journey PASSES end to end (two live turns; second turn recallable through the short-term overlay pre-consolidation; receipts current after consolidation). Codex journey SKIPS with the exact host gap named: entire 0.6.3-nightly's codex hooks are not loaded by codex 0.139, so no codex lifecycle events reach capture. Journey also caught a latent defect: a symlinked repository root (macOS /var vs /private/var) can resolve to two different repo keys across pipeline stages, splitting the brain identity; the harness canonicalizes, the underlying key resolution deserves a follow-up fix | Live-path proof recorded for Claude Code; Codex blocked on the entireio/cli host pairing, not on this repo; symlink identity fix queued as follow-up | `internal/cli/live_e2e_test.go` (opt-in; transcripts and credentials never retained; temp dirs auto-removed) |\n| 2026-08-08 | Correctness fixtures (not a retrieval-quality row): adversarial fixture pack from the 2026-08-07 audit, run against `a30036fe` (pre-fix) and the correctness branch | pre-fix vs post-fix behavior on: >16x filtered-candidate window, workspace graph/source leak + branch fan-out, old/new stable-ID across tiers, tombstone-then-read window, undeletable-store purge, overlay failure states, oversized-transcript expansion allocation | pre-fix baselines FAIL as the audit predicted: filtered query false-empties (`[]` with the in-scope hit seeded), tombstoned canary still served, workspace_graph appended to source=conversation; post-fix all fixtures pass on pure-Go and cgo suites, and the expansion fixture holds expansion under 4 MiB allocated for a 16 MiB transcript | Correctness corrections shipped in one PR off the Bugbot-fixes branch; no product claims, correctness contracts only | fixtures live in the repo test suite (`TestConversationFilteredCandidateWindow*`, `TestWorkspaceConversationSourceIsolation*`, `TestTwoTierStableIDReconciliation`, `TestExclusionReadGuard*`, `TestPurgeFailsNonZero*`, `TestShortTermOverlayStates*`, `TestConversationExpansionStreams*`); failing baselines in session scratchpad `r0-baselines/` |\n\n## Closed negatives — do not re-litigate without new evidence\n\n**Reopening discipline (worked example, 2026-06-10):** scan-cache v3 closed\n\"index request records\" as measured ranking noise with no consumer. Phase 2's\nhandoff packet and midtask mining became new consumers — new evidence — so v4\nreopened it *narrowly*: requests are extracted again for trajectory surfaces\nwhile the original noise finding stands untouched (both rankers still exclude\nthem from general ranking). Closed negatives are reopened by new consumers or\nnew measurements, never by forgetting why they closed.\n\n- **Query expansion:** early d≈0.47 was an n≈8 artifact; collapsed at n=121\n  (d=0.10, p=0.26). Stays opt-in.\n- **RRF fusion-weight tuning:** swept; all cells within noise. k0=60, equal\n  weight stands.\n- **Facts FTS5 BM25 as default:** parity, not better (1.43 vs 1.50). Opt-in.\n- **History coverage-gate relaxation (3-of-N → 2):** added filler-word noise,\n  regressed precision; BM25 is the fix, not gate tuning.\n- **Scoped-floor (recall floor via backfill facts):** dead end; backfill facts\n  don't help.\n- **Model2Vec fusion on history:** significantly *worse* than BM25 on precision\n  at production scale (t=−6.33 on 418k-record entire.io, t=−2.84 on entire-cli;\n  2026-06-12 capstone), with no useful/1k gain. The 06-11 midtask positive was a\n  sign-test artifact that didn't generalize. History fusion requires a\n  Gemma-class embedder; do not enable it with the built-in M2V.\n- **Conversation-exchange fusion (even with Gemma):** first read (2026-08-07,\n  dev-only n) traded exact-match precision for +1 paraphrase hit; the\n  displacement failure mode, on the arm's own 2 KiB request+response\n  projections. Fused ranking stays dark behind\n  `ENTIRE_BRAIN_CONVERSATION_FUSION`; reopen with request-weighted embedding\n  text and/or a larger pack, not by flipping the flag. UPDATE 2026-08-08:\n  reqw1 shipped as the embedding scheme (reverses the R@1 loss) but the flag\n  stays dark; two top-5 dropouts remain; next avenue is asymmetric fusion\n  weighting or a stricter semantic-only bar.\n\n## Adding a row\n\nWhen a measurement gates a ship/park decision, append it here the same day:\ndate, corpus + task count, what was compared, the headline number with its\nsignificance, the decision it served, and where the repro lives.\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"\n- `brain_delete_project` accepts only the bound repo's key. A foreign `repo_key`\n  is refused; the deletion is irreversible and `confirm=true` is no protection\n  against a prompt-injected agent that supplies it itself.\n- `brain_list_projects` returns only the bound project, not every locally\n  indexed repo's key, brain path, and index counts.\n- `brain_workspace_graph`, `brain_workspace_regressions`, and\n  `brain_workspace_review` refuse a workspace the bound repository is not a\n  member of, or one whose repos live outside the bound repository's parent\n  directory. Sibling checkouts under a common parent — `devenv/cli` alongside\n  `devenv/entiredb`, the layout `entire brain workspace add` produces — are in\n  scope without the opt-in.\n\nAn unbound server refuses project listing, deletion, and workspace tools by\ndefault. Workspace keys must match their local checkouts, and execution uses\nthe same manifest snapshot that passed the scope checks.\n\nSet `ENTIRE_BRAIN_MCP_ALLOW_CROSS_REPO=1` on the server to opt back into\ncross-repo behaviour (the sibling of `ENTIRE_BRAIN_MCP_ALLOW_ANY_PATH`, which\ndoes the same for `brain_index_repository`'s path argument). The refusal message\nalways names the variable. None of this touches the `entire brain ...` CLI: a\nhuman at a terminal keeps every cross-repo verb, gate unset.\n\n`brain_patterns` and `brain_patterns_status` are read-only pattern-corpus\ninspection tools. Skill formation is intentionally not exposed as an MCP write\ntool; use the explicit CLI flow `entire brain patterns skills form` when a human\nor authorized automation wants to synthesize a skill.\n# Recall threat model: prompt injection and secret retention\n\nScope: the conversational-memory and history recall surfaces (CLI retrieval\nverbs, MCP tools, brief, bundles/publish, logs, and the derived stores), per\nPhase 4 deliverable 7 of the conversational-memory plan. This documents what\nthe code enforces today, where the boundaries are, and the residual risks with\ntheir tracking state. It is a living document: change the code, change this.\n\n## Assets\n\n- **Captured transcripts** (exported copies under the brain's `sessions/`):\n  may contain secrets typed or pasted during sessions, hostile text copied\n  from the web or from repo content, and instruction-like text of any origin.\n- **Derived projections**: history index (classic records + conversation\n  exchange projections), FTS stores, vector stores, scan caches, pattern\n  episodes/corpus, durable facts, distill caches.\n- **Published artifacts**: brain bundles (semantic snapshots, overlays, facts).\n- **Receipts and logs**: serve receipts, watch output, MCP debug log.\n\n## Adversary channels and enforced boundaries\n\n### 1. Hostile content inside recalled history (prompt injection at recall)\n\nRecalled conversation text is attacker-influencable by construction: anything\na past session read (web pages, repo files, tool output) can plant\ninstruction-like text that later surfaces in retrieval.\n\nEnforced:\n\n- Every conversation result carries `verification_required: true` plus a\n  machine-readable `historical_conversation` caveat on every surface (CLI\n  JSON, MCP JSON, text rendering) stating recalled content is quoted data,\n  never instructions. The canary test proves an instruction-like string is\n  returned only inside this wrapper.\n- Tool and skill descriptions never instruct an agent to obey recalled\n  content; the recall skill's safety contract is test-locked\n  (`TestRecallSkillTemplatesEmbeddedAndSafe`).\n- Hidden reasoning, raw tool output, and injected wrapper/pseudo-user\n  messages are excluded from exchange text at extraction; harness noise (API\n  error envelopes, hook injections) is filtered.\n- `matched_terms` explainability exposes why weak matches surfaced, so\n  low-signal bait is diagnosable.\n# Release Blockers\n\nA register of release-gating findings from the PR #33 review (2026-06-11),\nkept next to the audit so a release decision can see what is open, what was\nfixed, and exactly why. The standard for this file is the eval ledger's:\nexplicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\n\n## RESOLVED AS CLAIM DEMOTION — B1: Answer-bearing query hints invalidated the old replay-lab proof\n\n**The claim under audit.** `docs/release_readiness_audit.md` previously treated\nthree replay-lab suites as citable proof that history/MCP/Radar context improved\nagent outcomes without handing over hidden validation or expected text. That\nattribution was unsupported.\n\n**The confound.** `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py` injects `brain_queries` into\nbrain/MCP-arm prompts only; the `no_brain` arm receives none. In the retained\npre-B1 suites, several `brain_queries` contained answer-bearing identifiers,\nhidden-test names, or near-verbatim hidden-validation strings. The old\ncomparison therefore measured *(answer-bearing hint + brain)* versus *(no hint,\nno brain)*, not brain value alone.\n\n**Fixes landed.**\n\n- `brain_query_leak_audit` now rejects answer-bearing `brain_queries` before a\n  panel can run. It checks code-shaped identifiers and verbatim 3+-word phrases\n  against hidden fix text and paths, expected files, hidden validation commands,\n  expected-string greps, hidden test names, and validation fixture contents.\n- All committed benchmark task queries that tripped the auditor were rewritten\n  to symptom-level retrieval terms. The all-task sweep now reports zero flagged\n  task files.\n- The retained evidence manifest is stricter again: even in `no_release_claim`\n  mode it requires zero hard integrity flags.\n- The old confounded retained suites were removed from\n  `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release` and replaced with clean reruns.\n\n**Clean rerun result (2026-06-11).** Item 3 is now complete: the three promoted\nsuites were rerun from a clean checkout with the sanitized task configs, four\nrepetitions per side, retained panel provenance, and host paths redacted before\ncommit. The independent audit now reports 3 suites, 24 records, 24/24 provenance\ncomplete, 0 hard integrity flags, 8 MCP-verified datapoints, 4 completed\nnamed-tool Radar datapoints, and 0 proof-ready comparisons.\n\n| Clean retained suite | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `release-candidate-entire-brain-schema-contract-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but noisy: pass rate 50% -> 75%, mean score 86.5 -> 87.75, `proof_ready=false`. |\n| `release-candidate-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.25 -> 91.25, `proof_ready=false`. |\n| `release-candidate-cli-radar-mcp-del-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.5 -> 90.5, `proof_ready=false`. |\n\n**Current release implication.** B1 is resolved as an integrity/confound blocker:\nthe retained release lane no longer contains answer-bearing query-hint artifacts.\nIt is still `no_release_claim`, because the clean reruns did not produce a\nproof-ready replay-lab lift. Any future agent-lift claim needs harder clean\nretained tasks that survive the proof-ready gate; the old numbers stay removed\nfrom the release story.\n\nOperationalization note: the literal \"any token\" wording from the review is not\nimplemented because it would false-flag ordinary symptom text. The enforced rule\nis code-shaped identifiers plus verbatim 3+-word phrases, with the known residual\nthat 1-2 word plain-English overlaps are not flagged.\n\n## RESOLVED — fixed during review on this branch\n\n**R1 — Eval label discipline orphaned the history-eval pipeline** (fixed in\n`15e7aaa`). `validateEvalTask` rejected `history-eval-gen` output and every\nretained task file; `eval-compare` hard-errored on its own default eval-gen\noutput. Fix separates ground-*truth* (same explicit labels, same source →\ncomparable) from evidence *grade* (human/judge-refined → claimable);\nhistory-eval now declares `provenance_silver`, legacy files default to it,\nand side-dependent truths (`source_match`, runtime judge) stay gated behind\n`--allow-proxy-comparison`. Covered by a new gen→load→run→compare seam test.\n\n**R2 — Retrieval panic on the loopback guard's own rejection path** (fixed in\n`15e7aaa`). `configuredEmbedder` dereferenced the nil returned for a\nnon-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBED_URL`; every `search`/`vsearch`/`query`\ncrashed in the exact scenario the guard hardens. Now degrades to the bundled\nModel2Vec embedder with a warning; regression test added.\n\n**R3 — Brain write-lock scoping** (fixed in `15e7aaa`). Export held the\nexclusive lock across the minutes-long transcript phase while every other\nuser times out at 10s — failing a concurrent distill's FINAL flush (an\nhours-long run killed at its last step) — and `openHistoryFTS` took the write\nlock on the query READ path, serializing all searches. Export now locks only\nthe shared-artifact phases; FTS opens fresh indexes lock-free and\ndouble-checks freshness under the lock only for rebuilds.\n\n**R4 — Silent full re-distill on upgrade** (fixed alongside this file). The\nfingerprint salt plus the stable-branch-dir rename invalidated every existing\ncache entry, and the shipped \"legacy key\" fallback could never match (a\nlegacy-format fingerprint never equals a salted one) — the first post-upgrade\nrun would re-distill the entire corpus (observed scale: ~14h of agent calls\nfor a 2,640-session brain). Fixed with lazy grandfathering: the legacy\nformula is kept genuinely computable (including pre-rename transcript paths),\na matching legacy entry counts as cached and is rewritten under the new\nkey/format on first touch, and the transcript path is no longer hashed into\nthe new fingerprint at all — storage layout is not identity, and hashing it\nre-invalidates the world on every future layout change. The filtered-session\ncarry-through, which copied legacy-format fingerprints under new-format keys\n(making them permanently unmatchable), now preserves entries under their own\nkeys. Covered by `TestDistillCacheGrandfathersLegacyEntries`, including the\nrenamed-branch-dir case and the changed-content negative.\n# P0 GA readiness — entire-graph + entire-brain + GraphMark\n\nA single, cross-repo checklist for the P0 General Availability of the local brain:\nthe semantic provider (`entire-graph`), the brain (`entire-brain`), and the eval\nharness (`GraphMark`). The standard here matches `docs/release-blockers.md` and\n`docs/release_readiness_audit.md`: explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\n\n## GA gate — everything below must hold on one aligned release SHA\n\n| # | Gate | State | Evidence |\n|---|------|-------|----------|\n| 1 | `entire-graph` module path is the org namespace | ✅ done | `go.mod` = `github.com/entireio/entire-graph` (migrated) |\n| 2 | `entire-graph` version stamped from a real tag | ✅ done | tag `v0.1.0`; `scripts/release.sh` injects `-X main.version=$(git describe --tags)` |\n| 3 | Provider schema is a frozen, pinnable GA contract | ✅ done | ADR 0001 — schema `1.x` (minor `1.1`), additive-only, tolerant readers |\n| 4 | Brain pins the provider at the live repo | ✅ done | `entire-plugin.yml` `repo_url` → `github.com/entireio/entire-graph` |\n| 5 | No-egress + deterministic golden coverage | ✅ exists | `doctor` `no_egress:true`; golden/provider/quality tests green (GA acceptance bar) |\n| 6 | `brain_*` MCP tool contract locked | ✅ exists | schemas `additionalProperties:false`, unknown-key rejection, named-tool auditability |\n| 7 | GraphMark wired as a regression gate | ✅ done | `GraphMark` CI: self-tests + significance no-drift; floor = 28/30 languages, 1148 vs 802 |\n| 8 | Phase-1 local-only boundary frozen as a guardrail | ✅ exists | stdio MCP only; `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` / `LOCAL_ONLY` documented |\n| 9 | Release blockers B1 + R1–R4 confirmed closed on RC SHA | ✅ done | `mise run release:evidence` on the RC SHA: 0 hard integrity flags, 24/24 records with required provenance. See \"GA cut — resolved\" §1 and `docs/release-blockers.md` |\n| 10 | Tagged `main` on `entire-graph` **and** `entire-brain`, aligned | ✅ done | both cut `v0.1.0` on the aligned GA SHA. See \"GA cut — resolved\" §2 and \"Provider compatibility since the GA cut\" below |\n| 11 | `no_release_claim` items resolved (proof or scoped-out) | ✅ resolved | see \"Claim posture\" below |\n\n## Compatibility matrix\n\n| Producer | Contract | Consumer | Rule |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `entire-graph` schema | `1.x` (ADR 0001) | `entire-brain` ingestion | accept any `1.x`, ignore unknown fields, warn on newer minor |\n| `entire-graph` provider | `provider_version` in manifest header | `entire-brain` refresh | recorded, not gated; used for provenance |\n| `GraphMark` harness | committed `*.score.json` + `stats_significance.py` | CI regression gate | significance report must regenerate byte-identical; corpus/harness changes must re-commit it |\n\nPinning guidance: brain consumers may pin the provider `>=1.0 <2.0`; a `2.0` is a\nbreaking change with a migration note and is out of the P0 `1.x` line.\n\n## Claim posture (honest — never overclaimed)\n\n- **Semantic usefulness — CLAIMABLE.** Backed by `GraphMark`: Entire beats the\n  comparison baseline on **28 of 30 top languages** at exact-McNemar p<0.05\n  (C# p=0.07 and PHP p=0.18 lead on rate but sit just under significance — more\n  scored repos, not a loss), overall **1,148 vs 802** correct (91% vs 64%,\n  p≈0), with Benjamini-Hochberg multiple-comparisons control. This is the first\n  broad, reproducible, in-repo-gated proof and supersedes the earlier single\n  narrow condition-level result.\n- **Distill wall-clock (>24h target-repo timing) — NO CLAIM.** Only ~2× local\n  proof (`audit_distill_perf.py`) exists; the >24h target-repo evidence was never\n  collected. GA makes **no distill-speed claim**; scoped out until measured.\n- **Durable-facts-vs-raw — NO CLAIM.** The four-arm harness exists but there are\n  **zero active durable facts**, so there is no paired proof. Facts ship as a\n  capability with **no comparative-quality claim** until seeded facts + paired\n  evidence land.\n\nThese match `docs/release_readiness_audit.md`; nothing here is asserted beyond its\nevidence.\n\n## Distribution\n\n- **P0 channel: signed release archives.** `entire-graph/scripts/release.sh` emits\n  per-OS/arch tarballs under `dist/` with `SHA256SUMS`; that is the GA artifact.\n  Install is via the Entire CLI plugin flow pinned at the tagged release.\n- **Marketplace / plugin-discovery listing: out of scope for P0**, tracked as a\n  post-GA follow-up.\n\n## GA cut — resolved\n\n1. ✅ **Release evidence gate passed.** `mise run release:evidence` on the RC SHA:\n   **0 hard integrity flags**, 24/24 records with required provenance (source\n   base/head + harness/config/tool hashes). B1 + R1–R4 hold.\n2. ✅ **Both repos tagged, aligned.** `entire-graph` `v0.1.0` and `entire-brain`\n   `v0.1.0` cut on the aligned GA SHA.\n3. ✅ **MCP surfaces verified independent** (no longer referenced-not-verified):\n   the brain stdio server (`entire brain mcp`, 34 `brain_*` tools) and the CLI's\n   hidden `entire mcp` (2 tools: `agent_help`, `entire_status`) are two separate\n   binaries with **disjoint tool namespaces, distinct `serverInfo`, no proxy, no\n   collision**. Decision: **intentionally separate** — brain owns the rich\n   memory/graph surface, the CLI owns a thin status/help surface for MCP-host\n   agents without a hook channel. The only divergences (framing: brain dual /\n   CLI NDJSON-only; fallback protocol `2024-11-05` vs `2025-06-18`; max frame\n   4 MiB vs 1 MiB) are cosmetic, cause no current-state breakage, and are\n   deferred to the P2 unified-MCP-surface work — not a P0 blocker.\n\n## Provider compatibility since the GA cut\n\nGate 10 pinned the aligned `v0.1.0` ↔ `v0.1.0` GA cut. `entire-graph` has since\nreleased `v0.2.0` (2026-07-16) and `v0.3.0` (2026-08-14) while `entire-brain`\nremains at `v0.1.0`. The tags are no longer numerically aligned; the **contract**\nstill is, and that is what gate 10 protects:\n\n- `entire-graph` `v0.3.0` still advertises `SchemaVersion = \"1.1\"`\n  (`internal/sem/provider.go`) — the same version cut at GA, and within the\n  additive-only `1.x` major that ADR 0001 freezes.\n- The emitted `record_type` set is unchanged: `file`, `symbol`, `relation`,\n  `external`, `summary` — all of which the brain's snapshot reader already\n  handles.\n- The brain consumes `entire graph snapshot` and `entire graph doctor` only. It\n  does not call `entire graph search`, so search-path work (multi-resolution\n  prose retrieval, `--single-resolution` / `--document-resolution`) does not\n  reach the brain's ingestion path.\n\nNo brain-side adaptation is required to run against `entire-graph` `v0.3.0`.\nRe-check this section on any `entire-graph` **major** bump, which by ADR 0001 is\nthe only release permitted to break the reader.\n\n**P0 GA status: gates 1–11 satisfied.** The local brain (entire-graph + entire-brain\n+ GraphMark) is at GA on the `v0.1.0` line.\n# Eval ledger\n\n> Naming note: recorded `search` and `vsearch` commands remain compatibility\n> aliases. Current usage is `query --keyword` and `query --semantic`; plain\n> `query` remains hybrid. Historical results below retain their original names.\n\nOne row per retrieval-quality or agent-outcome measurement that gated a decision. The task sets,\ncorpus snapshots, and metrics differ between rows — **numbers are comparable\nonly within a row's own baseline**, never across rows. Before claiming a\nregression or a win, find the row whose gate you are re-testing and reproduce\nits exact config; the source doc has the repro commands.\n\n| Date | Corpus / tasks | Comparison | Headline | Decision it gated | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-06-08 | entire-brain `main`, 179 facts, 16 provenance-labeled tasks (`facts eval-gen`, k=10) | lexical-only vs Model2Vec fused | lexical 0.86 → fused **1.50 useful/1k** (+76%); concept stratum 0 → 0.79 | Frozen Stage 0 baseline; any later embedder swap must beat 1.50 on this set. Also: facts FTS5 BM25 measured at parity (1.43), so BM25 ships **opt-in** (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_FACTS_BM25=1`), not default | `../alignment.md` (Stage 0); artifacts at `<brain>/eval/baseline-20260608/` |\n| 2026-06-08 | same 16-task set | Model2Vec fused vs EmbeddingGemma-300M (Q8_0, shell-to-local-server runner) | **1.80 useful/1k (+20%)**, precision 0.106, concept stratum 1.68 (2.1×); gain is reachability (three 0.00→~1.75 rescues), not uniform lift | Stage 1b embedder **quality gate: passed**. Runtime/distribution work still parked | `../alignment.md` (Stage 1b) |\n| 2026-06-08 | entire-brain (16 tasks) + podcasts (44 tasks), pooled n=60 | Model2Vec vs EmbeddingGemma, second repo | pooled 1.77 → **2.00 useful/1k (+14%)**; +13% on the non-meta repo | Confirms the Gemma gain is not a meta-domain artifact; right-sizes the effect from +20% to a moderate +14% | `../alignment.md` (multi-repo confirmation) |\n| 2026-06-08 | live 32k-record history index | substring scorer vs FTS5 BM25 (history) | `matches: null` defect fixed: BM25's IDF replaces the 3-of-N term-coverage gate; Model2Vec on history measured as **noise** (negative cosine separation), EmbeddingGemma separates (0.397 > 0.317) | History ships **BM25-only by default** (Stage 1a); a history semantic arm waits for the Stage 1b embedder | `../alignment.md` (Stage 1a findings) |\n| 2026-06-09 | entire-brain `main`, 930 facts, 17 deterministic tasks | frozen B0 baseline | lexical 1.063 useful/1k, semantic 1.013 | Appendix D (B1–B4) work measured against this snapshot | `durable_facts_handover.md` (B0) |\n| 2026-06-09 | pooled n=118 (17 entire-brain + 101 entire-cli tasks) | flat vs locus-**scoped** vs outline retrieval arms | scoped: **+59% useful/1k** (p=0.027 raw; marginal under Holm), −112 tokens (p<0.001), recall −0.029 (p=0.004); outline not a retrieval win (p=0.51) | B4 verdict: **scoped retrieval validated**; outline kept as a human-readable map, not a ranking mechanism; scoped-floor variant killed | `durable_facts_handover.md` (B4) |\n| 2026-06-09 | 121-task benchmark (potion-retrieval-32M) | lexical vs Model2Vec fused (shipped config) | **+0.459 useful/1k** (p=0.005, Holm-significant), precision +0.025 (p=0.013), no token cost | Phase D ship decision: semantic fusion **default-on** for `recall`/`brief` | `durable_facts_handover.md` (Phase D) |\n| 2026-06-10 | entire-brain live brain, **history layer**: 33.8k rankable records, 13 provenance-labeled tasks (`history-eval-gen`, k=10) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused (`history-eval` arms) | substring 0.315 → **BM25 0.927 useful/1k (2.9×)**, precision 0.062 → 0.146 — first quantitative confirmation of the shipped BM25 default. Cutoff sweep 0.15/0.30/0.50: **within noise** → the shipped 0.30 stands. Fused (Model2Vec) 1.219 (+31% over BM25), 4W/3L/6T — **directional only**: n=13 with 6 all-zero tasks leaves 7 informative pairs, far from significant. Tension with the 2026-06-08 \"M2V noise on history\" probe is real but explainable: that probe measured raw cosine separation on paraphrases; RRF fusion bounds how much a weak semantic arm can hurt while letting its agreements help | History eval harness landed (`history-eval-gen` / `history-eval`); cutoff question **closed**; history semantic arm **stays unshipped** pending an EmbeddingGemma run (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBEDDER=ollama … --arm fused`) and a second repo | this repo (`internal/cli/history_eval.go`); task set regenerable via `history-eval-gen` |\n\n| 2026-06-10 | three repos, **history layer**: entire-brain (13 tasks), podcasts (16), entire-cli (**882**, 267k records) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused vs **EmbeddingGemma-fused** (canonical GGUF via node-llama-cpp server) | useful/1k — podcasts: 1.128 / 1.554 / 1.731 / **2.108**; entire-brain: 0.315 / 0.927 / 1.219 / 0.978; entire-cli: 0.283 / 1.016 / 1.033 / **1.158**. At n=882: M2V-fused is **parity** with BM25 (+1.7% — the small-repo +31% was noise, consistent with the original M2V-noise probe), while **Gemma-fused is +14% (329W/248L/305T, sign test p=0.00075)** — the same +14% the facts layer measured, now decision-grade on history | **History semantic arm: validated with EmbeddingGemma, not with Model2Vec.** Production wiring (fused history arm when a Gemma embedder is configured; history vectors in vec0) is now justified but not yet built. BM25 default reconfirmed at scale (3.6× substring) | this repo (`history-eval` fused arm); per-repo JSONs regenerable |\n\n| 2026-06-10 | entire-brain live brain, **midtask stratum**: 33 tasks (20 midtask) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused, per stratum | midtask useful/1k: 0.317 / 0.631 / 0.881 — BM25's lift over substring is **smaller on midtask (2.0×)** than on opening concept queries (5.9×), and fusion helps midtask most in relative terms (+40% over BM25). n=20, directional | Mid-session questions are a real, harder stratum; powered confirmation queued on the entire-cli v4 re-scan and the entire.io capstone | this repo (`history-eval-gen --midtask`) |\n| 2026-06-11 | entire-cli v4 index (273k records, 6.2k requests), **1,522 tasks** incl. **632 midtask** | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused, per stratum, paired | midtask useful/1k: 0.260 / 0.709 / 0.737. BM25 over substring holds on every stratum (2.7×–5.1×) but is **weakest on midtask (2.7×)**. M2V-fused vs BM25: **overall parity (453W/425L, p=0.34)** — consistent with the three-repo finding — but **positive on the midtask stratum (181W/144L, p=0.040)**: even the weak embedder helps where questions are narrow and in-flight | Item 8 premise confirmed at power: the midtask stratum leans on semantics where opening requests do not. Evaluate retrieval levers against it before shipping hook-path defaults; the Gemma midtask read rides the entire.io capstone batch | this repo (`history-eval-gen` v4) |\n| 2026-06-12 | **capstone**: entire.io v4 (**418k records, 2,584 tasks**, 1,049 midtask) + entire-cli v4 (1,522 tasks, 632 midtask), paired per-task t-tests | BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused vs **EmbeddingGemma-fused**, first read at production scale | entire.io useful/1k: BM25 0.883 / M2V 0.857 / **Gemma 0.998 (+13%, t=7.08)**; precision: Gemma **+0.016 (t=7.68)** while **M2V −0.013 (t=−6.33)** — at 418k records the weak embedder costs significant precision and buys nothing. entire-cli replicates: Gemma +12.5% useful/1k (t=5.09), precision +0.017 (t=6.38); M2V precision **−0.007 (t=−2.84)**, useful/1k parity (t=0.73). Midtask: Gemma beats BM25 on both repos (t=5.19 eio / t=2.06 cli); the 06-11 cli M2V midtask positive does **not** generalize — eio midtask M2V is flat (t=0.33). Third independent ~+13% Gemma read (facts +14%, three-repo history +14%, capstone +13%/+12.5%) | **Item 9 verdict: ship the history fused arm gated on a configured Gemma-class embedder; Model2Vec fusion on history is a closed negative at scale.** BM25 stays the no-embedder default. (Substring arm abandoned mid-run: its per-task re-scoring is O(tasks×records) — 6.5h without finishing at this scale; its baseline is already established at 2.7–5.1× on three repos) | this repo (`history-eval`); artifacts in `~/.entire-brain-eval/` (regenerable) |\n| 2026-06-18 | entire-brain `main`, replay-lab clean correctness task (`entire-brain-clean-default-fact-merge-confidence`, a decided default whose value lives only in retained history), n=4/side, `claude:sonnet:high` | no_brain vs full_brain (history channel), **end-to-end agent validation pass-rate** | no_brain **0/4** → full_brain **4/4**; `brain_positive_stable`, `proof_ready=true` (pass-rate lift surviving drop-one); `audit_codex.py` 0 hard integrity flags, 16/16 provenance-backed. no_brain cannot recover the exact decided value; full_brain reads it from history and restores it | **First proof-ready replay-lab agent-lift.** Flips the history-channel correctness scope from `no_release_claim` to claimable; MCP/Radar/codex-runner/efficiency scopes stay no-claim. Co-located contract-checkpoint comparison saturated (both 4/4) | `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/replay-lab-clean/` (manifest + codex-audit-report); panel `p01-clean-proof-claude`; gate `mise run clean-proof:evidence` |\n| 2026-08-07 | entire-brain live brain, **conversation-exchange layer** (1,006 exchanges after dedupe): 22-task exact/paraphrase/failed/decision pack (v6 ids) + 10-task held paraphrase stratum, EmbeddingGemma via ollama (Intel CPU), dev-only n | conversation BM25 (search) vs BM25+Gemma RRF fusion (query) vs semantic-only (vsearch) | exact pack: lexical R@1 0.864 / R@5 1.000 / MRR 0.932 vs fused **0.773 / 0.955 / 0.864**; fusion displaced two rank-1 exact hits and dropped one paraphrase from rank 1 to unranked; held paraphrase stratum: lexical 4/10, fused **5/10** (+1), vsearch 5/10 with different coverage. Small n, one corpus, one embedder; directional, not significant | **Conversation fusion ships DARK behind ENTIRE_BRAIN_CONVERSATION_FUSION; conversation `query` stays BM25-only by default** (same eligibility discipline as history fusion: an arm turns on via a validated ledger row, not by existing). vsearch stays available as explicit semantic-only. Reopen with better embedding text (projection mixes request+response; consider request-weighted) and/or a larger pack | dev packs + scorer in session scratchpad (private; corpus identity); store `history/embeddings/conversation-vectors.sqlite` |\n| 2026-08-08 | entire-brain live brain post-consolidation (76,238 records; exchanges incl. the prior day's sessions), same 22-task exact pack + 10-task paraphrase stratum, EmbeddingGemma via ollama, dev-only n | conversation BM25 vs BM25+Gemma RRF fusion with **request-weighted embeddings** (`reqw1`: request line + 512 B response head, versioned store id) | lexical R@1 0.818 / R@5 1.000 / MRR 0.909 vs fused-reqw1 **0.909 / 0.909 / 0.909**; reqw1 REVERSES the mixed-text scheme's R@1 loss (fused now +0.091 over lexical; was −0.091) and keeps +1 paraphrase (5/10 vs 4/10), but two exact queries drop out of the top-5 entirely. Note the aging pack: the lexical baseline itself moved (0.864→0.818 R@1) as new sessions about the same topics joined the corpus | **reqw1 ships as the embedding scheme** (better fused profile, vsearch unchanged), but the fusion flag STAYS DARK: two complete top-5 dropouts on exact queries is still a real displacement cost at n=22. Next reopen avenue: asymmetric fusion weight (down-weight the semantic list) or a higher semantic-only calibration bar, plus a regenerated larger pack | dev packs + scorer in session scratchpad; store id `ollama:embeddinggemma:reqw1` |\n| 2026-08-08 | Live capture-loop journeys (sanctioned): real Claude Code (haiku) and Codex CLI sessions in isolated scratch repos under real `entire` capture (0.6.3-nightly), gated behind ENTIRE_BRAIN_LIVE_E2E=1 | full chain per journey: capture -> checkpoint fold on user commit -> incremental export -> delta recall BEFORE consolidation -> consolidation -> search/get/outline/receipts | Claude Code journey PASSES end to end (two live turns; second turn recallable through the short-term overlay pre-consolidation; receipts current after consolidation). Codex journey SKIPS with the exact host gap named: entire 0.6.3-nightly's codex hooks are not loaded by codex 0.139, so no codex lifecycle events reach capture. Journey also caught a latent defect: a symlinked repository root (macOS /var vs /private/var) can resolve to two different repo keys across pipeline stages, splitting the brain identity; the harness canonicalizes, the underlying key resolution deserves a follow-up fix | Live-path proof recorded for Claude Code; Codex blocked on the entireio/cli host pairing, not on this repo; symlink identity fix queued as follow-up | `internal/cli/live_e2e_test.go` (opt-in; transcripts and credentials never retained; temp dirs auto-removed) |\n| 2026-08-08 | Correctness fixtures (not a retrieval-quality row): adversarial fixture pack from the 2026-08-07 audit, run against `a30036fe` (pre-fix) and the correctness branch | pre-fix vs post-fix behavior on: >16x filtered-candidate window, workspace graph/source leak + branch fan-out, old/new stable-ID across tiers, tombstone-then-read window, undeletable-store purge, overlay failure states, oversized-transcript expansion allocation | pre-fix baselines FAIL as the audit predicted: filtered query false-empties (`[]` with the in-scope hit seeded), tombstoned canary still served, workspace_graph appended to source=conversation; post-fix all fixtures pass on pure-Go and cgo suites, and the expansion fixture holds expansion under 4 MiB allocated for a 16 MiB transcript | Correctness corrections shipped in one PR off the Bugbot-fixes branch; no product claims, correctness contracts only | fixtures live in the repo test suite (`TestConversationFilteredCandidateWindow*`, `TestWorkspaceConversationSourceIsolation*`, `TestTwoTierStableIDReconciliation`, `TestExclusionReadGuard*`, `TestPurgeFailsNonZero*`, `TestShortTermOverlayStates*`, `TestConversationExpansionStreams*`); failing baselines in session scratchpad `r0-baselines/` |\n\n## Closed negatives — do not re-litigate without new evidence\n\n**Reopening discipline (worked example, 2026-06-10):** scan-cache v3 closed\n\"index request records\" as measured ranking noise with no consumer. Phase 2's\nhandoff packet and midtask mining became new consumers — new evidence — so v4\nreopened it *narrowly*: requests are extracted again for trajectory surfaces\nwhile the original noise finding stands untouched (both rankers still exclude\nthem from general ranking). Closed negatives are reopened by new consumers or\nnew measurements, never by forgetting why they closed.\n\n- **Query expansion:** early d≈0.47 was an n≈8 artifact; collapsed at n=121\n  (d=0.10, p=0.26). Stays opt-in.\n- **RRF fusion-weight tuning:** swept; all cells within noise. k0=60, equal\n  weight stands.\n- **Facts FTS5 BM25 as default:** parity, not better (1.43 vs 1.50). Opt-in.\n- **History coverage-gate relaxation (3-of-N → 2):** added filler-word noise,\n  regressed precision; BM25 is the fix, not gate tuning.\n- **Scoped-floor (recall floor via backfill facts):** dead end; backfill facts\n  don't help.\n- **Model2Vec fusion on history:** significantly *worse* than BM25 on precision\n  at production scale (t=−6.33 on 418k-record entire.io, t=−2.84 on entire-cli;\n  2026-06-12 capstone), with no useful/1k gain. The 06-11 midtask positive was a\n  sign-test artifact that didn't generalize. History fusion requires a\n  Gemma-class embedder; do not enable it with the built-in M2V.\n- **Conversation-exchange fusion (even with Gemma):** first read (2026-08-07,\n  dev-only n) traded exact-match precision for +1 paraphrase hit; the\n  displacement failure mode, on the arm's own 2 KiB request+response\n  projections. Fused ranking stays dark behind\n  `ENTIRE_BRAIN_CONVERSATION_FUSION`; reopen with request-weighted embedding\n  text and/or a larger pack, not by flipping the flag. UPDATE 2026-08-08:\n  reqw1 shipped as the embedding scheme (reverses the R@1 loss) but the flag\n  stays dark; two top-5 dropouts remain; next avenue is asymmetric fusion\n  weighting or a stricter semantic-only bar.\n\n## Adding a row\n\nWhen a measurement gates a ship/park decision, append it here the same day:\ndate, corpus + task count, what was compared, the headline number with its\nsignificance, the decision it served, and where the repro lives.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":1250},"formatted_output":"\n- `brain_delete_project` accepts only the bound repo's key. A foreign `repo_key`\n  is refused; the deletion is irreversible and `confirm=true` is no protection\n  against a prompt-injected agent that supplies it itself.\n- `brain_list_projects` returns only the bound project, not every locally\n  indexed repo's key, brain path, and index counts.\n- `brain_workspace_graph`, `brain_workspace_regressions`, and\n  `brain_workspace_review` refuse a workspace the bound repository is not a\n  member of, or one whose repos live outside the bound repository's parent\n  directory. Sibling checkouts under a common parent — `devenv/cli` alongside\n  `devenv/entiredb`, the layout `entire brain workspace add` produces — are in\n  scope without the opt-in.\n\nAn unbound server refuses project listing, deletion, and workspace tools by\ndefault. Workspace keys must match their local checkouts, and execution uses\nthe same manifest snapshot that passed the scope checks.\n\nSet `ENTIRE_BRAIN_MCP_ALLOW_CROSS_REPO=1` on the server to opt back into\ncross-repo behaviour (the sibling of `ENTIRE_BRAIN_MCP_ALLOW_ANY_PATH`, which\ndoes the same for `brain_index_repository`'s path argument). The refusal message\nalways names the variable. None of this touches the `entire brain ...` CLI: a\nhuman at a terminal keeps every cross-repo verb, gate unset.\n\n`brain_patterns` and `brain_patterns_status` are read-only pattern-corpus\ninspection tools. Skill formation is intentionally not exposed as an MCP write\ntool; use the explicit CLI flow `entire brain patterns skills form` when a human\nor authorized automation wants to synthesize a skill.\n# Recall threat model: prompt injection and secret retention\n\nScope: the conversational-memory and history recall surfaces (CLI retrieval\nverbs, MCP tools, brief, bundles/publish, logs, and the derived stores), per\nPhase 4 deliverable 7 of the conversational-memory plan. This documents what\nthe code enforces today, where the boundaries are, and the residual risks with\ntheir tracking state. It is a living document: change the code, change this.\n\n## Assets\n\n- **Captured transcripts** (exported copies under the brain's `sessions/`):\n  may contain secrets typed or pasted during sessions, hostile text copied\n  from the web or from repo content, and instruction-like text of any origin.\n- **Derived projections**: history index (classic records + conversation\n  exchange projections), FTS stores, vector stores, scan caches, pattern\n  episodes/corpus, durable facts, distill caches.\n- **Published artifacts**: brain bundles (semantic snapshots, overlays, facts).\n- **Receipts and logs**: serve receipts, watch output, MCP debug log.\n\n## Adversary channels and enforced boundaries\n\n### 1. Hostile content inside recalled history (prompt injection at recall)\n\nRecalled conversation text is attacker-influencable by construction: anything\na past session read (web pages, repo files, tool output) can plant\ninstruction-like text that later surfaces in retrieval.\n\nEnforced:\n\n- Every conversation result carries `verification_required: true` plus a\n  machine-readable `historical_conversation` caveat on every surface (CLI\n  JSON, MCP JSON, text rendering) stating recalled content is quoted data,\n  never instructions. The canary test proves an instruction-like string is\n  returned only inside this wrapper.\n- Tool and skill descriptions never instruct an agent to obey recalled\n  content; the recall skill's safety contract is test-locked\n  (`TestRecallSkillTemplatesEmbeddedAndSafe`).\n- Hidden reasoning, raw tool output, and injected wrapper/pseudo-user\n  messages are excluded from exchange text at extraction; harness noise (API\n  error envelopes, hook injections) is filtered.\n- `matched_terms` explainability exposes why weak matches surfaced, so\n  low-signal bait is diagnosable.\n# Release Blockers\n\nA register of release-gating findings from the PR #33 review (2026-06-11),\nkept next to the audit so a release decision can see what is open, what was\nfixed, and exactly why. The standard for this file is the eval ledger's:\nexplicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\n\n## RESOLVED AS CLAIM DEMOTION — B1: Answer-bearing query hints invalidated the old replay-lab proof\n\n**The claim under audit.** `docs/release_readiness_audit.md` previously treated\nthree replay-lab suites as citable proof that history/MCP/Radar context improved\nagent outcomes without handing over hidden validation or expected text. That\nattribution was unsupported.\n\n**The confound.** `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py` injects `brain_queries` into\nbrain/MCP-arm prompts only; the `no_brain` arm receives none. In the retained\npre-B1 suites, several `brain_queries` contained answer-bearing identifiers,\nhidden-test names, or near-verbatim hidden-validation strings. The old\ncomparison therefore measured *(answer-bearing hint + brain)* versus *(no hint,\nno brain)*, not brain value alone.\n\n**Fixes landed.**\n\n- `brain_query_leak_audit` now rejects answer-bearing `brain_queries` before a\n  panel can run. It checks code-shaped identifiers and verbatim 3+-word phrases\n  against hidden fix text and paths, expected files, hidden validation commands,\n  expected-string greps, hidden test names, and validation fixture contents.\n- All committed benchmark task queries that tripped the auditor were rewritten\n  to symptom-level retrieval terms. The all-task sweep now reports zero flagged\n  task files.\n- The retained evidence manifest is stricter again: even in `no_release_claim`\n  mode it requires zero hard integrity flags.\n- The old confounded retained suites were removed from\n  `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release` and replaced with clean reruns.\n\n**Clean rerun result (2026-06-11).** Item 3 is now complete: the three promoted\nsuites were rerun from a clean checkout with the sanitized task configs, four\nrepetitions per side, retained panel provenance, and host paths redacted before\ncommit. The independent audit now reports 3 suites, 24 records, 24/24 provenance\ncomplete, 0 hard integrity flags, 8 MCP-verified datapoints, 4 completed\nnamed-tool Radar datapoints, and 0 proof-ready comparisons.\n\n| Clean retained suite | Outcome |\n|---|---|\n| `release-candidate-entire-brain-schema-contract-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but noisy: pass rate 50% -> 75%, mean score 86.5 -> 87.75, `proof_ready=false`. |\n| `release-candidate-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.25 -> 91.25, `proof_ready=false`. |\n| `release-candidate-cli-radar-mcp-del-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.5 -> 90.5, `proof_ready=false`. |\n\n**Current release implication.** B1 is resolved as an integrity/confound blocker:\nthe retained release lane no longer contains answer-bearing query-hint artifacts.\nIt is still `no_release_claim`, because the clean reruns did not produce a\nproof-ready replay-lab lift. Any future agent-lift claim needs harder clean\nretained tasks that survive the proof-ready gate; the old numbers stay removed\nfrom the release story.\n\nOperationalization note: the literal \"any token\" wording from the review is not\nimplemented because it would false-flag ordinary symptom text. The enforced rule\nis code-shaped identifiers plus verbatim 3+-word phrases, with the known residual\nthat 1-2 word plain-English overlaps are not flagged.\n\n## RESOLVED — fixed during review on this branch\n\n**R1 — Eval label discipline orphaned the history-eval pipeline** (fixed in\n`15e7aaa`). `validateEvalTask` rejected `history-eval-gen` output and every\nretained task file; `eval-compare` hard-errored on its own default eval-gen\noutput. Fix separates ground-*truth* (same explicit labels, same source →\ncomparable) from evidence *grade* (human/judge-refined → claimable);\nhistory-eval now declares `provenance_silver`, legacy files default to it,\nand side-dependent truths (`source_match`, runtime judge) stay gated behind\n`--allow-proxy-comparison`. Covered by a new gen→load→run→compare seam test.\n\n**R2 — Retrieval panic on the loopback guard's own rejection path** (fixed in\n`15e7aaa`). `configuredEmbedder` dereferenced the nil returned for a\nnon-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBED_URL`; every `search`/`vsearch`/`query`\ncrashed in the exact scenario the guard hardens. Now degrades to the bundled\nModel2Vec embedder with a warning; regression test added.\n\n**R3 — Brain write-lock scoping** (fixed in `15e7aaa`). Export held the\nexclusive lock across the minutes-long transcript phase while every other\nuser times out at 10s — failing a concurrent distill's FINAL flush (an\nhours-long run killed at its last step) — and `openHistoryFTS` took the write\nlock on the query READ path, serializing all searches. Export now locks only\nthe shared-artifact phases; FTS opens fresh indexes lock-free and\ndouble-checks freshness under the lock only for rebuilds.\n\n**R4 — Silent full re-distill on upgrade** (fixed alongside this file). The\nfingerprint salt plus the stable-branch-dir rename invalidated every existing\ncache entry, and the shipped \"legacy key\" fallback could never match (a\nlegacy-format fingerprint never equals a salted one) — the first post-upgrade\nrun would re-distill the entire corpus (observed scale: ~14h of agent calls\nfor a 2,640-session brain). Fixed with lazy grandfathering: the legacy\nformula is kept genuinely computable (including pre-rename transcript paths),\na matching legacy entry counts as cached and is rewritten under the new\nkey/format on first touch, and the transcript path is no longer hashed into\nthe new fingerprint at all — storage layout is not identity, and hashing it\nre-invalidates the world on every future layout change. The filtered-session\ncarry-through, which copied legacy-format fingerprints under new-format keys\n(making them permanently unmatchable), now preserves entries under their own\nkeys. Covered by `TestDistillCacheGrandfathersLegacyEntries`, including the\nrenamed-branch-dir case and the changed-content negative.\n# P0 GA readiness — entire-graph + entire-brain + GraphMark\n\nA single, cross-repo checklist for the P0 General Availability of the local brain:\nthe semantic provider (`entire-graph`), the brain (`entire-brain`), and the eval\nharness (`GraphMark`). The standard here matches `docs/release-blockers.md` and\n`docs/release_readiness_audit.md`: explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\n\n## GA gate — everything below must hold on one aligned release SHA\n\n| # | Gate | State | Evidence |\n|---|------|-------|----------|\n| 1 | `entire-graph` module path is the org namespace | ✅ done | `go.mod` = `github.com/entireio/entire-graph` (migrated) |\n| 2 | `entire-graph` version stamped from a real tag | ✅ done | tag `v0.1.0`; `scripts/release.sh` injects `-X main.version=$(git describe --tags)` |\n| 3 | Provider schema is a frozen, pinnable GA contract | ✅ done | ADR 0001 — schema `1.x` (minor `1.1`), additive-only, tolerant readers |\n| 4 | Brain pins the provider at the live repo | ✅ done | `entire-plugin.yml` `repo_url` → `github.com/entireio/entire-graph` |\n| 5 | No-egress + deterministic golden coverage | ✅ exists | `doctor` `no_egress:true`; golden/provider/quality tests green (GA acceptance bar) |\n| 6 | `brain_*` MCP tool contract locked | ✅ exists | schemas `additionalProperties:false`, unknown-key rejection, named-tool auditability |\n| 7 | GraphMark wired as a regression gate | ✅ done | `GraphMark` CI: self-tests + significance no-drift; floor = 28/30 languages, 1148 vs 802 |\n| 8 | Phase-1 local-only boundary frozen as a guardrail | ✅ exists | stdio MCP only; `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` / `LOCAL_ONLY` documented |\n| 9 | Release blockers B1 + R1–R4 confirmed closed on RC SHA | ✅ done | `mise run release:evidence` on the RC SHA: 0 hard integrity flags, 24/24 records with required provenance. See \"GA cut — resolved\" §1 and `docs/release-blockers.md` |\n| 10 | Tagged `main` on `entire-graph` **and** `entire-brain`, aligned | ✅ done | both cut `v0.1.0` on the aligned GA SHA. See \"GA cut — resolved\" §2 and \"Provider compatibility since the GA cut\" below |\n| 11 | `no_release_claim` items resolved (proof or scoped-out) | ✅ resolved | see \"Claim posture\" below |\n\n## Compatibility matrix\n\n| Producer | Contract | Consumer | Rule |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `entire-graph` schema | `1.x` (ADR 0001) | `entire-brain` ingestion | accept any `1.x`, ignore unknown fields, warn on newer minor |\n| `entire-graph` provider | `provider_version` in manifest header | `entire-brain` refresh | recorded, not gated; used for provenance |\n| `GraphMark` harness | committed `*.score.json` + `stats_significance.py` | CI regression gate | significance report must regenerate byte-identical; corpus/harness changes must re-commit it |\n\nPinning guidance: brain consumers may pin the provider `>=1.0 <2.0`; a `2.0` is a\nbreaking change with a migration note and is out of the P0 `1.x` line.\n\n## Claim posture (honest — never overclaimed)\n\n- **Semantic usefulness — CLAIMABLE.** Backed by `GraphMark`: Entire beats the\n  comparison baseline on **28 of 30 top languages** at exact-McNemar p<0.05\n  (C# p=0.07 and PHP p=0.18 lead on rate but sit just under significance — more\n  scored repos, not a loss), overall **1,148 vs 802** correct (91% vs 64%,\n  p≈0), with Benjamini-Hochberg multiple-comparisons control. This is the first\n  broad, reproducible, in-repo-gated proof and supersedes the earlier single\n  narrow condition-level result.\n- **Distill wall-clock (>24h target-repo timing) — NO CLAIM.** Only ~2× local\n  proof (`audit_distill_perf.py`) exists; the >24h target-repo evidence was never\n  collected. GA makes **no distill-speed claim**; scoped out until measured.\n- **Durable-facts-vs-raw — NO CLAIM.** The four-arm harness exists but there are\n  **zero active durable facts**, so there is no paired proof. Facts ship as a\n  capability with **no comparative-quality claim** until seeded facts + paired\n  evidence land.\n\nThese match `docs/release_readiness_audit.md`; nothing here is asserted beyond its\nevidence.\n\n## Distribution\n\n- **P0 channel: signed release archives.** `entire-graph/scripts/release.sh` emits\n  per-OS/arch tarballs under `dist/` with `SHA256SUMS`; that is the GA artifact.\n  Install is via the Entire CLI plugin flow pinned at the tagged release.\n- **Marketplace / plugin-discovery listing: out of scope for P0**, tracked as a\n  post-GA follow-up.\n\n## GA cut — resolved\n\n1. ✅ **Release evidence gate passed.** `mise run release:evidence` on the RC SHA:\n   **0 hard integrity flags**, 24/24 records with required provenance (source\n   base/head + harness/config/tool hashes). B1 + R1–R4 hold.\n2. ✅ **Both repos tagged, aligned.** `entire-graph` `v0.1.0` and `entire-brain`\n   `v0.1.0` cut on the aligned GA SHA.\n3. ✅ **MCP surfaces verified independent** (no longer referenced-not-verified):\n   the brain stdio server (`entire brain mcp`, 34 `brain_*` tools) and the CLI's\n   hidden `entire mcp` (2 tools: `agent_help`, `entire_status`) are two separate\n   binaries with **disjoint tool namespaces, distinct `serverInfo`, no proxy, no\n   collision**. Decision: **intentionally separate** — brain owns the rich\n   memory/graph surface, the CLI owns a thin status/help surface for MCP-host\n   agents without a hook channel. The only divergences (framing: brain dual /\n   CLI NDJSON-only; fallback protocol `2024-11-05` vs `2025-06-18`; max frame\n   4 MiB vs 1 MiB) are cosmetic, cause no current-state breakage, and are\n   deferred to the P2 unified-MCP-surface work — not a P0 blocker.\n\n## Provider compatibility since the GA cut\n\nGate 10 pinned the aligned `v0.1.0` ↔ `v0.1.0` GA cut. `entire-graph` has since\nreleased `v0.2.0` (2026-07-16) and `v0.3.0` (2026-08-14) while `entire-brain`\nremains at `v0.1.0`. The tags are no longer numerically aligned; the **contract**\nstill is, and that is what gate 10 protects:\n\n- `entire-graph` `v0.3.0` still advertises `SchemaVersion = \"1.1\"`\n  (`internal/sem/provider.go`) — the same version cut at GA, and within the\n  additive-only `1.x` major that ADR 0001 freezes.\n- The emitted `record_type` set is unchanged: `file`, `symbol`, `relation`,\n  `external`, `summary` — all of which the brain's snapshot reader already\n  handles.\n- The brain consumes `entire graph snapshot` and `entire graph doctor` only. It\n  does not call `entire graph search`, so search-path work (multi-resolution\n  prose retrieval, `--single-resolution` / `--document-resolution`) does not\n  reach the brain's ingestion path.\n\nNo brain-side adaptation is required to run against `entire-graph` `v0.3.0`.\nRe-check this section on any `entire-graph` **major** bump, which by ADR 0001 is\nthe only release permitted to break the reader.\n\n**P0 GA status: gates 1–11 satisfied.** The local brain (entire-graph + entire-brain\n+ GraphMark) is at GA on the `v0.1.0` line.\n# Eval ledger\n\n> Naming note: recorded `search` and `vsearch` commands remain compatibility\n> aliases. Current usage is `query --keyword` and `query --semantic`; plain\n> `query` remains hybrid. Historical results below retain their original names.\n\nOne row per retrieval-quality or agent-outcome measurement that gated a decision. The task sets,\ncorpus snapshots, and metrics differ between rows — **numbers are comparable\nonly within a row's own baseline**, never across rows. Before claiming a\nregression or a win, find the row whose gate you are re-testing and reproduce\nits exact config; the source doc has the repro commands.\n\n| Date | Corpus / tasks | Comparison | Headline | Decision it gated | Source |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2026-06-08 | entire-brain `main`, 179 facts, 16 provenance-labeled tasks (`facts eval-gen`, k=10) | lexical-only vs Model2Vec fused | lexical 0.86 → fused **1.50 useful/1k** (+76%); concept stratum 0 → 0.79 | Frozen Stage 0 baseline; any later embedder swap must beat 1.50 on this set. Also: facts FTS5 BM25 measured at parity (1.43), so BM25 ships **opt-in** (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_FACTS_BM25=1`), not default | `../alignment.md` (Stage 0); artifacts at `<brain>/eval/baseline-20260608/` |\n| 2026-06-08 | same 16-task set | Model2Vec fused vs EmbeddingGemma-300M (Q8_0, shell-to-local-server runner) | **1.80 useful/1k (+20%)**, precision 0.106, concept stratum 1.68 (2.1×); gain is reachability (three 0.00→~1.75 rescues), not uniform lift | Stage 1b embedder **quality gate: passed**. Runtime/distribution work still parked | `../alignment.md` (Stage 1b) |\n| 2026-06-08 | entire-brain (16 tasks) + podcasts (44 tasks), pooled n=60 | Model2Vec vs EmbeddingGemma, second repo | pooled 1.77 → **2.00 useful/1k (+14%)**; +13% on the non-meta repo | Confirms the Gemma gain is not a meta-domain artifact; right-sizes the effect from +20% to a moderate +14% | `../alignment.md` (multi-repo confirmation) |\n| 2026-06-08 | live 32k-record history index | substring scorer vs FTS5 BM25 (history) | `matches: null` defect fixed: BM25's IDF replaces the 3-of-N term-coverage gate; Model2Vec on history measured as **noise** (negative cosine separation), EmbeddingGemma separates (0.397 > 0.317) | History ships **BM25-only by default** (Stage 1a); a history semantic arm waits for the Stage 1b embedder | `../alignment.md` (Stage 1a findings) |\n| 2026-06-09 | entire-brain `main`, 930 facts, 17 deterministic tasks | frozen B0 baseline | lexical 1.063 useful/1k, semantic 1.013 | Appendix D (B1–B4) work measured against this snapshot | `durable_facts_handover.md` (B0) |\n| 2026-06-09 | pooled n=118 (17 entire-brain + 101 entire-cli tasks) | flat vs locus-**scoped** vs outline retrieval arms | scoped: **+59% useful/1k** (p=0.027 raw; marginal under Holm), −112 tokens (p<0.001), recall −0.029 (p=0.004); outline not a retrieval win (p=0.51) | B4 verdict: **scoped retrieval validated**; outline kept as a human-readable map, not a ranking mechanism; scoped-floor variant killed | `durable_facts_handover.md` (B4) |\n| 2026-06-09 | 121-task benchmark (potion-retrieval-32M) | lexical vs Model2Vec fused (shipped config) | **+0.459 useful/1k** (p=0.005, Holm-significant), precision +0.025 (p=0.013), no token cost | Phase D ship decision: semantic fusion **default-on** for `recall`/`brief` | `durable_facts_handover.md` (Phase D) |\n| 2026-06-10 | entire-brain live brain, **history layer**: 33.8k rankable records, 13 provenance-labeled tasks (`history-eval-gen`, k=10) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused (`history-eval` arms) | substring 0.315 → **BM25 0.927 useful/1k (2.9×)**, precision 0.062 → 0.146 — first quantitative confirmation of the shipped BM25 default. Cutoff sweep 0.15/0.30/0.50: **within noise** → the shipped 0.30 stands. Fused (Model2Vec) 1.219 (+31% over BM25), 4W/3L/6T — **directional only**: n=13 with 6 all-zero tasks leaves 7 informative pairs, far from significant. Tension with the 2026-06-08 \"M2V noise on history\" probe is real but explainable: that probe measured raw cosine separation on paraphrases; RRF fusion bounds how much a weak semantic arm can hurt while letting its agreements help | History eval harness landed (`history-eval-gen` / `history-eval`); cutoff question **closed**; history semantic arm **stays unshipped** pending an EmbeddingGemma run (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBEDDER=ollama … --arm fused`) and a second repo | this repo (`internal/cli/history_eval.go`); task set regenerable via `history-eval-gen` |\n\n| 2026-06-10 | three repos, **history layer**: entire-brain (13 tasks), podcasts (16), entire-cli (**882**, 267k records) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused vs **EmbeddingGemma-fused** (canonical GGUF via node-llama-cpp server) | useful/1k — podcasts: 1.128 / 1.554 / 1.731 / **2.108**; entire-brain: 0.315 / 0.927 / 1.219 / 0.978; entire-cli: 0.283 / 1.016 / 1.033 / **1.158**. At n=882: M2V-fused is **parity** with BM25 (+1.7% — the small-repo +31% was noise, consistent with the original M2V-noise probe), while **Gemma-fused is +14% (329W/248L/305T, sign test p=0.00075)** — the same +14% the facts layer measured, now decision-grade on history | **History semantic arm: validated with EmbeddingGemma, not with Model2Vec.** Production wiring (fused history arm when a Gemma embedder is configured; history vectors in vec0) is now justified but not yet built. BM25 default reconfirmed at scale (3.6× substring) | this repo (`history-eval` fused arm); per-repo JSONs regenerable |\n\n| 2026-06-10 | entire-brain live brain, **midtask stratum**: 33 tasks (20 midtask) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused, per stratum | midtask useful/1k: 0.317 / 0.631 / 0.881 — BM25's lift over substring is **smaller on midtask (2.0×)** than on opening concept queries (5.9×), and fusion helps midtask most in relative terms (+40% over BM25). n=20, directional | Mid-session questions are a real, harder stratum; powered confirmation queued on the entire-cli v4 re-scan and the entire.io capstone | this repo (`history-eval-gen --midtask`) |\n| 2026-06-11 | entire-cli v4 index (273k records, 6.2k requests), **1,522 tasks** incl. **632 midtask** | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused, per stratum, paired | midtask useful/1k: 0.260 / 0.709 / 0.737. BM25 over substring holds on every stratum (2.7×–5.1×) but is **weakest on midtask (2.7×)**. M2V-fused vs BM25: **overall parity (453W/425L, p=0.34)** — consistent with the three-repo finding — but **positive on the midtask stratum (181W/144L, p=0.040)**: even the weak embedder helps where questions are narrow and in-flight | Item 8 premise confirmed at power: the midtask stratum leans on semantics where opening requests do not. Evaluate retrieval levers against it before shipping hook-path defaults; the Gemma midtask read rides the entire.io capstone batch | this repo (`history-eval-gen` v4) |\n| 2026-06-12 | **capstone**: entire.io v4 (**418k records, 2,584 tasks**, 1,049 midtask) + entire-cli v4 (1,522 tasks, 632 midtask), paired per-task t-tests | BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused vs **EmbeddingGemma-fused**, first read at production scale | entire.io useful/1k: BM25 0.883 / M2V 0.857 / **Gemma 0.998 (+13%, t=7.08)**; precision: Gemma **+0.016 (t=7.68)** while **M2V −0.013 (t=−6.33)** — at 418k records the weak embedder costs significant precision and buys nothing. entire-cli replicates: Gemma +12.5% useful/1k (t=5.09), precision +0.017 (t=6.38); M2V precision **−0.007 (t=−2.84)**, useful/1k parity (t=0.73). Midtask: Gemma beats BM25 on both repos (t=5.19 eio / t=2.06 cli); the 06-11 cli M2V midtask positive does **not** generalize — eio midtask M2V is flat (t=0.33). Third independent ~+13% Gemma read (facts +14%, three-repo history +14%, capstone +13%/+12.5%) | **Item 9 verdict: ship the history fused arm gated on a configured Gemma-class embedder; Model2Vec fusion on history is a closed negative at scale.** BM25 stays the no-embedder default. (Substring arm abandoned mid-run: its per-task re-scoring is O(tasks×records) — 6.5h without finishing at this scale; its baseline is already established at 2.7–5.1× on three repos) | this repo (`history-eval`); artifacts in `~/.entire-brain-eval/` (regenerable) |\n| 2026-06-18 | entire-brain `main`, replay-lab clean correctness task (`entire-brain-clean-default-fact-merge-confidence`, a decided default whose value lives only in retained history), n=4/side, `claude:sonnet:high` | no_brain vs full_brain (history channel), **end-to-end agent validation pass-rate** | no_brain **0/4** → full_brain **4/4**; `brain_positive_stable`, `proof_ready=true` (pass-rate lift surviving drop-one); `audit_codex.py` 0 hard integrity flags, 16/16 provenance-backed. no_brain cannot recover the exact decided value; full_brain reads it from history and restores it | **First proof-ready replay-lab agent-lift.** Flips the history-channel correctness scope from `no_release_claim` to claimable; MCP/Radar/codex-runner/efficiency scopes stay no-claim. Co-located contract-checkpoint comparison saturated (both 4/4) | `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/replay-lab-clean/` (manifest + codex-audit-report); panel `p01-clean-proof-claude`; gate `mise run clean-proof:evidence` |\n| 2026-08-07 | entire-brain live brain, **conversation-exchange layer** (1,006 exchanges after dedupe): 22-task exact/paraphrase/failed/decision pack (v6 ids) + 10-task held paraphrase stratum, EmbeddingGemma via ollama (Intel CPU), dev-only n | conversation BM25 (search) vs BM25+Gemma RRF fusion (query) vs semantic-only (vsearch) | exact pack: lexical R@1 0.864 / R@5 1.000 / MRR 0.932 vs fused **0.773 / 0.955 / 0.864**; fusion displaced two rank-1 exact hits and dropped one paraphrase from rank 1 to unranked; held paraphrase stratum: lexical 4/10, fused **5/10** (+1), vsearch 5/10 with different coverage. Small n, one corpus, one embedder; directional, not significant | **Conversation fusion ships DARK behind ENTIRE_BRAIN_CONVERSATION_FUSION; conversation `query` stays BM25-only by default** (same eligibility discipline as history fusion: an arm turns on via a validated ledger row, not by existing). vsearch stays available as explicit semantic-only. Reopen with better embedding text (projection mixes request+response; consider request-weighted) and/or a larger pack | dev packs + scorer in session scratchpad (private; corpus identity); store `history/embeddings/conversation-vectors.sqlite` |\n| 2026-08-08 | entire-brain live brain post-consolidation (76,238 records; exchanges incl. the prior day's sessions), same 22-task exact pack + 10-task paraphrase stratum, EmbeddingGemma via ollama, dev-only n | conversation BM25 vs BM25+Gemma RRF fusion with **request-weighted embeddings** (`reqw1`: request line + 512 B response head, versioned store id) | lexical R@1 0.818 / R@5 1.000 / MRR 0.909 vs fused-reqw1 **0.909 / 0.909 / 0.909**; reqw1 REVERSES the mixed-text scheme's R@1 loss (fused now +0.091 over lexical; was −0.091) and keeps +1 paraphrase (5/10 vs 4/10), but two exact queries drop out of the top-5 entirely. Note the aging pack: the lexical baseline itself moved (0.864→0.818 R@1) as new sessions about the same topics joined the corpus | **reqw1 ships as the embedding scheme** (better fused profile, vsearch unchanged), but the fusion flag STAYS DARK: two complete top-5 dropouts on exact queries is still a real displacement cost at n=22. Next reopen avenue: asymmetric fusion weight (down-weight the semantic list) or a higher semantic-only calibration bar, plus a regenerated larger pack | dev packs + scorer in session scratchpad; store id `ollama:embeddinggemma:reqw1` |\n| 2026-08-08 | Live capture-loop journeys (sanctioned): real Claude Code (haiku) and Codex CLI sessions in isolated scratch repos under real `entire` capture (0.6.3-nightly), gated behind ENTIRE_BRAIN_LIVE_E2E=1 | full chain per journey: capture -> checkpoint fold on user commit -> incremental export -> delta recall BEFORE consolidation -> consolidation -> search/get/outline/receipts | Claude Code journey PASSES end to end (two live turns; second turn recallable through the short-term overlay pre-consolidation; receipts current after consolidation). Codex journey SKIPS with the exact host gap named: entire 0.6.3-nightly's codex hooks are not loaded by codex 0.139, so no codex lifecycle events reach capture. Journey also caught a latent defect: a symlinked repository root (macOS /var vs /private/var) can resolve to two different repo keys across pipeline stages, splitting the brain identity; the harness canonicalizes, the underlying key resolution deserves a follow-up fix | Live-path proof recorded for Claude Code; Codex blocked on the entireio/cli host pairing, not on this repo; symlink identity fix queued as follow-up | `internal/cli/live_e2e_test.go` (opt-in; transcripts and credentials never retained; temp dirs auto-removed) |\n| 2026-08-08 | Correctness fixtures (not a retrieval-quality row): adversarial fixture pack from the 2026-08-07 audit, run against `a30036fe` (pre-fix) and the correctness branch | pre-fix vs post-fix behavior on: >16x filtered-candidate window, workspace graph/source leak + branch fan-out, old/new stable-ID across tiers, tombstone-then-read window, undeletable-store purge, overlay failure states, oversized-transcript expansion allocation | pre-fix baselines FAIL as the audit predicted: filtered query false-empties (`[]` with the in-scope hit seeded), tombstoned canary still served, workspace_graph appended to source=conversation; post-fix all fixtures pass on pure-Go and cgo suites, and the expansion fixture holds expansion under 4 MiB allocated for a 16 MiB transcript | Correctness corrections shipped in one PR off the Bugbot-fixes branch; no product claims, correctness contracts only | fixtures live in the repo test suite (`TestConversationFilteredCandidateWindow*`, `TestWorkspaceConversationSourceIsolation*`, `TestTwoTierStableIDReconciliation`, `TestExclusionReadGuard*`, `TestPurgeFailsNonZero*`, `TestShortTermOverlayStates*`, `TestConversationExpansionStreams*`); failing baselines in session scratchpad `r0-baselines/` |\n\n## Closed negatives — do not re-litigate without new evidence\n\n**Reopening discipline (worked example, 2026-06-10):** scan-cache v3 closed\n\"index request records\" as measured ranking noise with no consumer. Phase 2's\nhandoff packet and midtask mining became new consumers — new evidence — so v4\nreopened it *narrowly*: requests are extracted again for trajectory surfaces\nwhile the original noise finding stands untouched (both rankers still exclude\nthem from general ranking). Closed negatives are reopened by new consumers or\nnew measurements, never by forgetting why they closed.\n\n- **Query expansion:** early d≈0.47 was an n≈8 artifact; collapsed at n=121\n  (d=0.10, p=0.26). Stays opt-in.\n- **RRF fusion-weight tuning:** swept; all cells within noise. k0=60, equal\n  weight stands.\n- **Facts FTS5 BM25 as default:** parity, not better (1.43 vs 1.50). Opt-in.\n- **History coverage-gate relaxation (3-of-N → 2):** added filler-word noise,\n  regressed precision; BM25 is the fix, not gate tuning.\n- **Scoped-floor (recall floor via backfill facts):** dead end; backfill facts\n  don't help.\n- **Model2Vec fusion on history:** significantly *worse* than BM25 on precision\n  at production scale (t=−6.33 on 418k-record entire.io, t=−2.84 on entire-cli;\n  2026-06-12 capstone), with no useful/1k gain. The 06-11 midtask positive was a\n  sign-test artifact that didn't generalize. History fusion requires a\n  Gemma-class embedder; do not enable it with the built-in M2V.\n- **Conversation-exchange fusion (even with Gemma):** first read (2026-08-07,\n  dev-only n) traded exact-match precision for +1 paraphrase hit; the\n  displacement failure mode, on the arm's own 2 KiB request+response\n  projections. Fused ranking stays dark behind\n  `ENTIRE_BRAIN_CONVERSATION_FUSION`; reopen with request-weighted embedding\n  text and/or a larger pack, not by flipping the flag. UPDATE 2026-08-08:\n  reqw1 shipped as the embedding scheme (reverses the R@1 loss) but the flag\n  stays dark; two top-5 dropouts remain; next avenue is asymmetric fusion\n  weighting or a stricter semantic-only bar.\n\n## Adding a row\n\nWhen a measurement gates a ship/park decision, append it here the same day:\ndate, corpus + task count, what was compared, the headline number with its\nsignificance, the decision it served, and where the repro lives.\n"},"started_at_ms":1789840021269,"completed_at_ms":1789840021269}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T17:47:01.272Z","ordinal":7746,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9","turn_id":"01a0ba4f-3944-7ce3-88ac-4c7975e84b1b","session_id":"01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9","root_turn_id":"01a0ba4f-3944-7ce3-88ac-4c7975e84b1b","response_id":"resp_0cb48b2b18d09e75016aaeca8e3ba487d282470921016e60dc","usage":{"input_tokens":58115,"cached_input_tokens":48640,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":92,"reasoning_output_tokens":9,"total_tokens":58207},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":77917977,"cached_input_tokens":74615936,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":182080,"reasoning_output_tokens":15170,"total_tokens":78100057},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":143802996,"cached_input_tokens":137187968,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":366879,"reasoning_output_tokens":36547,"total_tokens":144169875}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T17:47:01.325Z","ordinal":7747,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0bac7-574d-7e92-9c1b-68d0cbf51535","call_id":"call_4DPLQ0Al65rsslVjjJqEuwvp","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"57d3f1\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000125,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":8346,\"output\":\"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8346)\\nTotal output lines: 346\\n\\n\\n- `brain_delete_project` accepts only the bound repo's key. A foreign `repo_key`\\n  is refused; the deletion is irreversible and `confirm=true` is no protection\\n  against a prompt-injected agent that supplies it itself.\\n- `brain_list_projects` returns only the bound project, not every locally\\n  indexed repo's key, brain path, and index counts.\\n- `brain_workspace_graph`, `brain_workspace_regressions`, and\\n  `brain_workspace_review` refuse a workspace the bound repository is not a\\n  member of, or one whose repos live outside the bound repository's parent\\n  directory. Sibling checkouts under a common parent — `devenv/cli` alongside\\n  `devenv/entiredb`, the layout `entire brain workspace add` produces — are in\\n  scope without the opt-in.\\n\\nAn unbound server refuses project listing, deletion, and workspace tools by\\ndefault. Workspace keys must match their local checkouts, and execution uses\\nthe same manifest snapshot that passed the scope checks.\\n\\nSet `ENTIRE_BRAIN_MCP_ALLOW_CROSS_REPO=1` on the server to opt back into\\ncross-repo behaviour (the sibling of `ENTIRE_BRAIN_MCP_ALLOW_ANY_PATH`, which\\ndoes the same for `brain_index_repository`'s path argument). The refusal message\\nalways names the variable. None of this touches the `entire brain ...` CLI: a\\nhuman at a terminal keeps every cross-repo verb, gate unset.\\n\\n`brain_patterns` and `brain_patterns_status` are read-only pattern-corpus\\ninspection tools. Skill formation is intentionally not exposed as an MCP write\\ntool; use the explicit CLI flow `entire brain patterns skills form` when a human\\nor authorized automation wants to synthesize a skill.\\n# Recall threat model: prompt injection and secret retention\\n\\nScope: the conversational-memory and history recall surfaces (CLI retrieval\\nverbs, MCP tools, brief, bundles/publish, logs, and the derived stores), per\\nPhase 4 deliverable 7 of the conversational-memory plan. This documents what\\nthe code enforces today, where the boundaries are, and the residual risks with\\ntheir tracking state. It is a living document: change the code, change this.\\n\\n## Assets\\n\\n- **Captured transcripts** (exported copies under the brain's `sessions/`):\\n  may contain secrets typed or pasted during sessions, hostile text copied\\n  from the web or from repo content, and instruction-like text of any origin.\\n- **Derived projections**: history index (classic records + conversation\\n  exchange projections), FTS stores, vector stores, scan caches, pattern\\n  episodes/corpus, durable facts, distill caches.\\n- **Published artifacts**: brain bundles (semantic snapshots, overlays, facts).\\n- **Receipts and logs**: serve receipts, watch output, MCP debug log.\\n\\n## Adversary channels and enforced boundaries\\n\\n### 1. Hostile content inside recalled history (prompt injection at recall)\\n\\nRecalled conversation text is attacker-influencable by construction: anything\\na past session read (web pages, repo files, tool output) can plant\\ninstruction-like text that later surfaces in retrieval.\\n\\nEnforced:\\n\\n- Every conversation result carries `verification_required: true` plus a\\n  machine-readable `historical_conversation` caveat on every surface (CLI\\n  JSON, MCP JSON, text rendering) stating recalled content is quoted data,\\n  never instructions. The canary test proves an instruction-like string is\\n  returned only inside this wrapper.\\n- Tool and skill descriptions never instruct an agent to obey recalled\\n  content; the recall skill's safety contract is test-locked\\n  (`TestRecallSkillTemplatesEmbeddedAndSafe`).\\n- Hidden reasoning, raw tool output, and injected wrapper/pseudo-user\\n  messages are excluded from exchange text at extraction; harness noise (API\\n  error envelopes, hook injections) is filtered.\\n- `matched_terms` explainability exposes why weak matches surfaced, so\\n  low-signal bait is diagnosable.\\n# Release Blockers\\n\\nA register of release-gating findings from the PR #33 review (2026-06-11),\\nkept next to the audit so a release decision can see what is open, what was\\nfixed, and exactly why. The standard for this file is the eval ledger's:\\nexplicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\\n\\n## RESOLVED AS CLAIM DEMOTION — B1: Answer-bearing query hints invalidated the old replay-lab proof\\n\\n**The claim under audit.** `docs/release_readiness_audit.md` previously treated\\nthree replay-lab suites as citable proof that history/MCP/Radar context improved\\nagent outcomes without handing over hidden validation or expected text. That\\nattribution was unsupported.\\n\\n**The confound.** `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py` injects `brain_queries` into\\nbrain/MCP-arm prompts only; the `no_brain` arm receives none. In the retained\\npre-B1 suites, several `brain_queries` contained answer-bearing identifiers,\\nhidden-test names, or near-verbatim hidden-validation strings. The old\\ncomparison therefore measured *(answer-bearing hint + brain)* versus *(no hint,\\nno brain)*, not brain value alone.\\n\\n**Fixes landed.**\\n\\n- `brain_query_leak_audit` now rejects answer-bearing `brain_queries` before a\\n  panel can run. It checks code-shaped identifiers and verbatim 3+-word phrases\\n  against hidden fix text and paths, expected files, hidden validation commands,\\n  expected-string greps, hidden test names, and validation fixture contents.\\n- All committed benchmark task queries that tripped the auditor were rewritten\\n  to symptom-level retrieval terms. The all-task sweep now reports zero flagged\\n  task files.\\n- The retained evidence manifest is stricter again: even in `no_release_claim`\\n  mode it requires zero hard integrity flags.\\n- The old confounded retained suites were removed from\\n  `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/release` and replaced with clean reruns.\\n\\n**Clean rerun result (2026-06-11).** Item 3 is now complete: the three promoted\\nsuites were rerun from a clean checkout with the sanitized task configs, four\\nrepetitions per side, retained panel provenance, and host paths redacted before\\ncommit. The independent audit now reports 3 suites, 24 records, 24/24 provenance\\ncomplete, 0 hard integrity flags, 8 MCP-verified datapoints, 4 completed\\nnamed-tool Radar datapoints, and 0 proof-ready comparisons.\\n\\n| Clean retained suite | Outcome |\\n|---|---|\\n| `release-candidate-entire-brain-schema-contract-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but noisy: pass rate 50% -> 75%, mean score 86.5 -> 87.75, `proof_ready=false`. |\\n| `release-candidate-entire-cli-mcp-manual-attribution-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.25 -> 91.25, `proof_ready=false`. |\\n| `release-candidate-cli-radar-mcp-del-clean-20260611T0412Z` | Audit-clean but saturated/negative: both arms passed 100%, mean score 94.5 -> 90.5, `proof_ready=false`. |\\n\\n**Current release implication.** B1 is resolved as an integrity/confound blocker:\\nthe retained release lane no longer contains answer-bearing query-hint artifacts.\\nIt is still `no_release_claim`, because the clean reruns did not produce a\\nproof-ready replay-lab lift. Any future agent-lift claim needs harder clean\\nretained tasks that survive the proof-ready gate; the old numbers stay removed\\nfrom the release story.\\n\\nOperationalization note: the literal \\\"any token\\\" wording from the review is not\\nimplemented because it would false-flag ordinary symptom text. The enforced rule\\nis code-shaped identifiers plus verbatim 3+-word phrases, with the known residual\\nthat 1-2 word plain-English overlaps are not flagged.\\n\\n## RESOLVED — fixed during review on this branch\\n\\n**R1 — Eval label discipline orphaned the history-eval pipeline** (fixed in\\n`15e7aaa`). `validateEvalTask` rejected `history-eval-gen` output and every\\nretained task file; `eval-compare` hard-errored on its own default eval-gen\\noutput. Fix separates ground-*truth* (same explicit labels, same source →\\ncomparable) from evidence *grade* (human/judge-refined → claimable);\\nhistory-eval now declares `provenance_silver`, legacy files default to it,\\nand side-dependent truths (`source_match`, runtime judge) stay gated behind\\n`--allow-proxy-comparison`. Covered by a new gen→load→run→compare seam test.\\n\\n**R2 — Retrieval panic on the loopback guard's own rejection path** (fixed in\\n`15e7aaa`). `configuredEmbedder` dereferenced the nil returned for a\\nnon-loopback `ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBED_URL`; every `search`/`vsearch`/`query`\\ncrashed in the exact scenario the guard hardens. Now degrades to the bundled\\nModel2Vec embedder with a warning; regression test added.\\n\\n**R3 — Brain write-lock scoping** (fixed in `15e7aaa`). Export held the\\nexclusive lock across the minutes-long transcript phase while every other\\nuser times out at 10s — failing a concurrent distill's FINAL flush (an\\nhours-long run killed at its last step) — and `openHistoryFTS` took the write\\nlock on the query READ path, serializing all searches. Export now locks only\\nthe shared-artifact phases; FTS opens fresh indexes lock-free and\\ndouble-checks freshness under the lock only for rebuilds.\\n\\n**R4 — Silent full re-distill on upgrade** (fixed alongside this file). The\\nfingerprint salt plus the stable-branch-dir rename invalidated every existing\\ncache entry, and the shipped \\\"legacy key\\\" fallback could never match (a\\nlegacy-format fingerprint never equals a salted one) — the first post-upgrade\\nrun would re-distill the entire corpus (observed scale: ~14h of agent calls\\nfor a 2,640-session brain). Fixed with lazy grandfathering: the legacy\\nformula is kept genuinely computable (including pre-rename transcript paths),\\na matching legacy entry counts as cached and is rewritten under the new\\nkey/format on first touch, and the transcript path is no longer hashed into\\nthe new fingerprint at all — storage layout is not identity, and hashing it\\nre-invalidates the world on every future layout change. The filtered-session\\ncarry-through, which copied legacy-format fingerprints under new-format keys\\n(making them permanently unmatchable), now preserves entries under their own\\nkeys. Covered by `TestDistillCacheGrandfathersLegacyEntries`, including the\\nrenamed-branch-dir case and the changed-content negative.\\n# P0 GA readiness — entire-graph + entire-brain + GraphMark\\n\\nA single, cross-repo checklist for the P0 General Availability of the local brain:\\nthe semantic provider (`entire-graph`), the brain (`entire-brain`), and the eval\\nharness (`GraphMark`). The standard here matches `docs/release-blockers.md` and\\n`docs/release_readiness_audit.md`: explicit claims, exact evidence, no euphemism.\\n\\n## GA gate — everything below must hold on one aligned release SHA\\n\\n| # | Gate | State | Evidence |\\n|---|------|-------|----------|\\n| 1 | `entire-graph` module path is the org namespace | ✅ done | `go.mod` = `github.com/entireio/entire-graph` (migrated) |\\n| 2 | `entire-graph` version stamped from a real tag | ✅ done | tag `v0.1.0`; `scripts/release.sh` injects `-X main.version=$(git describe --tags)` |\\n| 3 | Provider schema is a frozen, pinnable GA contract | ✅ done | ADR 0001 — schema `1.x` (minor `1.1`), additive-only, tolerant readers |\\n| 4 | Brain pins the provider at the live repo | ✅ done | `entire-plugin.yml` `repo_url` → `github.com/entireio/entire-graph` |\\n| 5 | No-egress + deterministic golden coverage | ✅ exists | `doctor` `no_egress:true`; golden/provider/quality tests green (GA acceptance bar) |\\n| 6 | `brain_*` MCP tool contract locked | ✅ exists | schemas `additionalProperties:false`, unknown-key rejection, named-tool auditability |\\n| 7 | GraphMark wired as a regression gate | ✅ done | `GraphMark` CI: self-tests + significance no-drift; floor = 28/30 languages, 1148 vs 802 |\\n| 8 | Phase-1 local-only boundary frozen as a guardrail | ✅ exists | stdio MCP only; `ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` / `LOCAL_ONLY` documented |\\n| 9 | Release blockers B1 + R1–R4 confirmed closed on RC SHA | ✅ done | `mise run release:evidence` on the RC SHA: 0 hard integrity flags, 24/24 records with required provenance. See \\\"GA cut — resolved\\\" §1 and `docs/release-blockers.md` |\\n| 10 | Tagged `main` on `entire-graph` **and** `entire-brain`, aligned | ✅ done | both cut `v0.1.0` on the aligned GA SHA. See \\\"GA cut — resolved\\\" §2 and \\\"Provider compatibility since the GA cut\\\" below |\\n| 11 | `no_release_claim` items resolved (proof or scoped-out) | ✅ resolved | see \\\"Claim posture\\\" below |\\n\\n## Compatibility matrix\\n\\n| Producer | Contract | Consumer | Rule |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| `entire-graph` schema | `1.x` (ADR 0001) | `entire-brain` ingestion | accept any `1.x`, ignore unknown fields, warn on newer minor |\\n| `entire-graph` provider | `provider_version` in manifest header | `entire-brain` refresh | recorded, not gated; used for provenance |\\n| `GraphMark` harness | committed `*.score.json` + `stats_significance.py` | CI regression gate | significance report must regenerate byte-identical; corpus/harness changes must re-commit it |\\n\\nPinning guidance: brain consumers may pin the provider `>=1.0 <2.0`; a `2.0` is a\\nbreaking change with a migration note and is out of the P0 `1.x` line.\\n\\n## Claim posture (honest — never overclaimed)\\n\\n- **Semantic usefulness — CLAIMABLE.** Backed by `GraphMark`: Entire beats the\\n  comparison baseline on **28 of 30 top languages** at exact-McNemar p<0.05\\n  (C# p=0.07 and PHP p=0.18 lead on rate but sit just under significance — more\\n  scored repos, not a loss), overall **1,148 vs 802** correct (91% vs 64%,\\n  p≈0), with Benjamini-Hochberg multiple-comparisons control. This is the first\\n  broad, reproducible, in-repo-gated proof and supersedes the earlier single\\n  narrow condition-level result.\\n- **Distill wall-clock (>24h target-repo timing) — NO CLAIM.** Only ~2× local\\n  proof (`audit_distill_perf.py`) exists; the >24h target-repo evidence was never\\n  collected. GA makes **no distill-speed claim**; scoped out until measured.\\n- **Durable-facts-vs-raw — NO CLAIM.** The four-arm harness exists but there are\\n  **zero active durable facts**, so there is no paired proof. Facts ship as a\\n  capability with **no comparative-quality claim** until seeded facts + p…1346 tokens truncated…n B0 baseline | lexical 1.063 useful/1k, semantic 1.013 | Appendix D (B1–B4) work measured against this snapshot | `durable_facts_handover.md` (B0) |\\n| 2026-06-09 | pooled n=118 (17 entire-brain + 101 entire-cli tasks) | flat vs locus-**scoped** vs outline retrieval arms | scoped: **+59% useful/1k** (p=0.027 raw; marginal under Holm), −112 tokens (p<0.001), recall −0.029 (p=0.004); outline not a retrieval win (p=0.51) | B4 verdict: **scoped retrieval validated**; outline kept as a human-readable map, not a ranking mechanism; scoped-floor variant killed | `durable_facts_handover.md` (B4) |\\n| 2026-06-09 | 121-task benchmark (potion-retrieval-32M) | lexical vs Model2Vec fused (shipped config) | **+0.459 useful/1k** (p=0.005, Holm-significant), precision +0.025 (p=0.013), no token cost | Phase D ship decision: semantic fusion **default-on** for `recall`/`brief` | `durable_facts_handover.md` (Phase D) |\\n| 2026-06-10 | entire-brain live brain, **history layer**: 33.8k rankable records, 13 provenance-labeled tasks (`history-eval-gen`, k=10) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused (`history-eval` arms) | substring 0.315 → **BM25 0.927 useful/1k (2.9×)**, precision 0.062 → 0.146 — first quantitative confirmation of the shipped BM25 default. Cutoff sweep 0.15/0.30/0.50: **within noise** → the shipped 0.30 stands. Fused (Model2Vec) 1.219 (+31% over BM25), 4W/3L/6T — **directional only**: n=13 with 6 all-zero tasks leaves 7 informative pairs, far from significant. Tension with the 2026-06-08 \\\"M2V noise on history\\\" probe is real but explainable: that probe measured raw cosine separation on paraphrases; RRF fusion bounds how much a weak semantic arm can hurt while letting its agreements help | History eval harness landed (`history-eval-gen` / `history-eval`); cutoff question **closed**; history semantic arm **stays unshipped** pending an EmbeddingGemma run (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBEDDER=ollama … --arm fused`) and a second repo | this repo (`internal/cli/history_eval.go`); task set regenerable via `history-eval-gen` |\\n\\n| 2026-06-10 | three repos, **history layer**: entire-brain (13 tasks), podcasts (16), entire-cli (**882**, 267k records) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused vs **EmbeddingGemma-fused** (canonical GGUF via node-llama-cpp server) | useful/1k — podcasts: 1.128 / 1.554 / 1.731 / **2.108**; entire-brain: 0.315 / 0.927 / 1.219 / 0.978; entire-cli: 0.283 / 1.016 / 1.033 / **1.158**. At n=882: M2V-fused is **parity** with BM25 (+1.7% — the small-repo +31% was noise, consistent with the original M2V-noise probe), while **Gemma-fused is +14% (329W/248L/305T, sign test p=0.00075)** — the same +14% the facts layer measured, now decision-grade on history | **History semantic arm: validated with EmbeddingGemma, not with Model2Vec.** Production wiring (fused history arm when a Gemma embedder is configured; history vectors in vec0) is now justified but not yet built. BM25 default reconfirmed at scale (3.6× substring) | this repo (`history-eval` fused arm); per-repo JSONs regenerable |\\n\\n| 2026-06-10 | entire-brain live brain, **midtask stratum**: 33 tasks (20 midtask) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused, per stratum | midtask useful/1k: 0.317 / 0.631 / 0.881 — BM25's lift over substring is **smaller on midtask (2.0×)** than on opening concept queries (5.9×), and fusion helps midtask most in relative terms (+40% over BM25). n=20, directional | Mid-session questions are a real, harder stratum; powered confirmation queued on the entire-cli v4 re-scan and the entire.io capstone | this repo (`history-eval-gen --midtask`) |\\n| 2026-06-11 | entire-cli v4 index (273k records, 6.2k requests), **1,522 tasks** incl. **632 midtask** | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused, per stratum, paired | midtask useful/1k: 0.260 / 0.709 / 0.737. BM25 over substring holds on every stratum (2.7×–5.1×) but is **weakest on midtask (2.7×)**. M2V-fused vs BM25: **overall parity (453W/425L, p=0.34)** — consistent with the three-repo finding — but **positive on the midtask stratum (181W/144L, p=0.040)**: even the weak embedder helps where questions are narrow and in-flight | Item 8 premise confirmed at power: the midtask stratum leans on semantics where opening requests do not. Evaluate retrieval levers against it before shipping hook-path defaults; the Gemma midtask read rides the entire.io capstone batch | this repo (`history-eval-gen` v4) |\\n| 2026-06-12 | **capstone**: entire.io v4 (**418k records, 2,584 tasks**, 1,049 midtask) + entire-cli v4 (1,522 tasks, 632 midtask), paired per-task t-tests | BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused vs **EmbeddingGemma-fused**, first read at production scale | entire.io useful/1k: BM25 0.883 / M2V 0.857 / **Gemma 0.998 (+13%, t=7.08)**; precision: Gemma **+0.016 (t=7.68)** while **M2V −0.013 (t=−6.33)** — at 418k records the weak embedder costs significant precision and buys nothing. entire-cli replicates: Gemma +12.5% useful/1k (t=5.09), precision +0.017 (t=6.38); M2V precision **−0.007 (t=−2.84)**, useful/1k parity (t=0.73). Midtask: Gemma beats BM25 on both repos (t=5.19 eio / t=2.06 cli); the 06-11 cli M2V midtask positive does **not** generalize — eio midtask M2V is flat (t=0.33). Third independent ~+13% Gemma read (facts +14%, three-repo history +14%, capstone +13%/+12.5%) | **Item 9 verdict: ship the history fused arm gated on a configured Gemma-class embedder; Model2Vec fusion on history is a closed negative at scale.** BM25 stays the no-embedder default. (Substring arm abandoned mid-run: its per-task re-scoring is O(tasks×records) — 6.5h without finishing at this scale; its baseline is already established at 2.7–5.1× on three repos) | this repo (`history-eval`); artifacts in `~/.entire-brain-eval/` (regenerable) |\\n| 2026-06-18 | entire-brain `main`, replay-lab clean correctness task (`entire-brain-clean-default-fact-merge-confidence`, a decided default whose value lives only in retained history), n=4/side, `claude:sonnet:high` | no_brain vs full_brain (history channel), **end-to-end agent validation pass-rate** | no_brain **0/4** → full_brain **4/4**; `brain_positive_stable`, `proof_ready=true` (pass-rate lift surviving drop-one); `audit_codex.py` 0 hard integrity flags, 16/16 provenance-backed. no_brain cannot recover the exact decided value; full_brain reads it from history and restores it | **First proof-ready replay-lab agent-lift.** Flips the history-channel correctness scope from `no_release_claim` to claimable; MCP/Radar/codex-runner/efficiency scopes stay no-claim. Co-located contract-checkpoint comparison saturated (both 4/4) | `benchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/replay-lab-clean/` (manifest + codex-audit-report); panel `p01-clean-proof-claude`; gate `mise run clean-proof:evidence` |\\n| 2026-08-07 | entire-brain live brain, **conversation-exchange layer** (1,006 exchanges after dedupe): 22-task exact/paraphrase/failed/decision pack (v6 ids) + 10-task held paraphrase stratum, EmbeddingGemma via ollama (Intel CPU), dev-only n | conversation BM25 (search) vs BM25+Gemma RRF fusion (query) vs semantic-only (vsearch) | exact pack: lexical R@1 0.864 / R@5 1.000 / MRR 0.932 vs fused **0.773 / 0.955 / 0.864**; fusion displaced two rank-1 exact hits and dropped one paraphrase from rank 1 to unranked; held paraphrase stratum: lexical 4/10, fused **5/10** (+1), vsearch 5/10 with different coverage. Small n, one corpus, one embedder; directional, not significant | **Conversation fusion ships DARK behind ENTIRE_BRAIN_CONVERSATION_FUSION; conversation `query` stays BM25-only by default** (same eligibility discipline as history fusion: an arm turns on via a validated ledger row, not by existing). vsearch stays available as explicit semantic-only. Reopen with better embedding text (projection mixes request+response; consider request-weighted) and/or a larger pack | dev packs + scorer in session scratchpad (private; corpus identity); store `history/embeddings/conversation-vectors.sqlite` |\\n| 2026-08-08 | entire-brain live brain post-consolidation (76,238 records; exchanges incl. the prior day's sessions), same 22-task exact pack + 10-task paraphrase stratum, EmbeddingGemma via ollama, dev-only n | conversation BM25 vs BM25+Gemma RRF fusion with **request-weighted embeddings** (`reqw1`: request line + 512 B response head, versioned store id) | lexical R@1 0.818 / R@5 1.000 / MRR 0.909 vs fused-reqw1 **0.909 / 0.909 / 0.909**; reqw1 REVERSES the mixed-text scheme's R@1 loss (fused now +0.091 over lexical; was −0.091) and keeps +1 paraphrase (5/10 vs 4/10), but two exact queries drop out of the top-5 entirely. Note the aging pack: the lexical baseline itself moved (0.864→0.818 R@1) as new sessions about the same topics joined the corpus | **reqw1 ships as the embedding scheme** (better fused profile, vsearch unchanged), but the fusion flag STAYS DARK: two complete top-5 dropouts on exact queries is still a real displacement cost at n=22. Next reopen avenue: asymmetric fusion weight (down-weight the semantic list) or a higher semantic-only calibration bar, plus a regenerated larger pack | dev packs + scorer in session scratchpad; store id `ollama:embeddinggemma:reqw1` |\\n| 2026-08-08 | Live capture-loop journeys (sanctioned): real Claude Code (haiku) and Codex CLI sessions in isolated scratch repos under real `entire` capture (0.6.3-nightly), gated behind ENTIRE_BRAIN_LIVE_E2E=1 | full chain per journey: capture -> checkpoint fold on user commit -> incremental export -> delta recall BEFORE consolidation -> consolidation -> search/get/outline/receipts | Claude Code journey PASSES end to end (two live turns; second turn recallable through the short-term overlay pre-consolidation; receipts current after consolidation). Codex journey SKIPS with the exact host gap named: entire 0.6.3-nightly's codex hooks are not loaded by codex 0.139, so no codex lifecycle events reach capture. Journey also caught a latent defect: a symlinked repository root (macOS /var vs /private/var) can resolve to two different repo keys across pipeline stages, splitting the brain identity; the harness canonicalizes, the underlying key resolution deserves a follow-up fix | Live-path proof recorded for Claude Code; Codex blocked on the entireio/cli host pairing, not on this repo; symlink identity fix queued as follow-up | `internal/cli/live_e2e_test.go` (opt-in; transcripts and credentials never retained; temp dirs auto-removed) |\\n| 2026-08-08 | Correctness fixtures (not a retrieval-quality row): adversarial fixture pack from the 2026-08-07 audit, run against `a30036fe` (pre-fix) and the correctness branch | pre-fix vs post-fix behavior on: >16x filtered-candidate window, workspace graph/source leak + branch fan-out, old/new stable-ID across tiers, tombstone-then-read window, undeletable-store purge, overlay failure states, oversized-transcript expansion allocation | pre-fix baselines FAIL as the audit predicted: filtered query false-empties (`[]` with the in-scope hit seeded), tombstoned canary still served, workspace_graph appended to source=conversation; post-fix all fixtures pass on pure-Go and cgo suites, and the expansion fixture holds expansion under 4 MiB allocated for a 16 MiB transcript | Correctness corrections shipped in one PR off the Bugbot-fixes branch; no product claims, correctness contracts only | fixtures live in the repo test suite (`TestConversationFilteredCandidateWindow*`, `TestWorkspaceConversationSourceIsolation*`, `TestTwoTierStableIDReconciliation`, `TestExclusionReadGuard*`, `TestPurgeFailsNonZero*`, `TestShortTermOverlayStates*`, `TestConversationExpansionStreams*`); failing baselines in session scratchpad `r0-baselines/` |\\n\\n## Closed negatives — do not re-litigate without new evidence\\n\\n**Reopening discipline (worked example, 2026-06-10):** scan-cache v3 closed\\n\\\"index request records\\\" as measured ranking noise with no consumer. Phase 2's\\nhandoff packet and midtask mining became new consumers — new evidence — so v4\\nreopened it *narrowly*: requests are extracted again for trajectory surfaces\\nwhile the original noise finding stands untouched (both rankers still exclude\\nthem from general ranking). Closed negatives are reopened by new consumers or\\nnew measurements, never by forgetting why they closed.\\n\\n- **Query expansion:** early d≈0.47 was an n≈8 artifact; collapsed at n=121\\n  (d=0.10, p=0.26). Stays opt-in.\\n- **RRF fusion-weight tuning:** swept; all cells within noise. k0=60, equal\\n  weight stands.\\n- **Facts FTS5 BM25 as default:** parity, not better (1.43 vs 1.50). Opt-in.\\n- **History coverage-gate relaxation (3-of-N → 2):** added filler-word noise,\\n  regressed precision; BM25 is the fix, not gate tuning.\\n- **Scoped-floor (recall floor via backfill facts):** dead end; backfill facts\\n  don't help.\\n- **Model2Vec fusion on history:** significantly *worse* than BM25 on precision\\n  at production scale (t=−6.33 on 418k-record entire.io, t=−2.84 on entire-cli;\\n  2026-06-12 capstone), with no useful/1k gain. The 06-11 midtask positive was a\\n  sign-test artifact that didn't generalize. History fusion requires a\\n  Gemma-class embedder; do not enable it with the built-in M2V.\\n- **Conversation-exchange fusion (even with Gemma):** first read (2026-08-07,\\n  dev-only n) traded exact-match precision for +1 paraphrase hit; the\\n  displacement failure mode, on the arm's own 2 KiB request+response\\n  projections. Fused ranking stays dark behind\\n  `ENTIRE_BRAIN_CONVERSATION_FUSION`; reopen with request-weighted embedding\\n  text and/or a larger pack, not by flipping the flag. UPDATE 2026-08-08:\\n  reqw1 shipped as the embedding scheme (reverses the R@1 loss) but the flag\\n  stays dark; two top-5 dropouts remain; next avenue is asymmetric fusion\\n  weighting or a stricter semantic-only bar.\\n\\n## Adding a row\\n\\nWhen a measurement gates a ship/park decision, append it here the same day:\\ndate, corpus + task count, what was compared, the headline number with its\\nsignificance, the decision it served, and where the repro lives.\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0ba4f-3944-7ce3-88ac-4c7975e84b1b","create_time":1789840021.325832}}}
