er cannot weaken competitor, without a controlled comparison; preregistration similarly asserts contamination cannot create a false positive despite possible treatment interaction. Treat these as unsupported methodological assurances, not observed runtime outcomes. Paper outline puts validity check after confirmatory although preregistration requires it before; uses 6 arms while primary protocol lists 5. Maintenance version string hashes config only despite declaring every seal change a new version; same config/count can label distinct seals identically. These are documentation/design inconsistencies. Main benchmark README retains stale release gate thresholds (2 suites/16 records/2 proof-ready/history+mcp) versus actual manifest (3/24/0/no claim). Re-executed retained audits: clean history 20 records/zero hard flags/one proof-ready PASS; legacy release 24 records/16 historical task-hash flags explicitly allowed under no-claim manifest, no proof-ready; both distill reports FAIL current distill_cmd.go hash binding. Saved generated reports outside repository.\\\\n')\\nprint('Added documentation coverage',len(names),'total inspected',sum(x['review_status']=='source-inspected' for x in r))\\nPY\",\"max_output_tokens\":1000})).output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0ba4f-3944-7ce3-88ac-4c7975e84b1b","create_time":1789840184.386449}}}
