{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T17:57:51.739Z","ordinal":8135,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9","turn_id":"01a0ba4f-3944-7ce3-88ac-4c7975e84b1b","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_0cb48b2b18d09e75016aaecd1d802487d286a1042f057479a7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"The main quality problem is uneven contract enforcement: the normal paths have substantial test coverage, but several failure paths can lose data, serve stale state, or report stronger evidence than they actually establish. The documentation also contains conflicting status claims and unsupported assurances. I’m keeping those separate from confirmed runtime defects.\n"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1789840669606,"completed_at_ms":1789840671739}}
