{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T20:00:46.029Z","ordinal":8436,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0bb41-c9cd-7972-b381-297020526993","call_id":"call_wP9EL0R0mVTZARQwzLPyvUbb","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"85a357\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.1704395,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":2228,\"output\":\"{\\n  \\\"command\\\": \\\"entire session attach\\\",\\n  \\\"short\\\": \\\"Attach an existing agent session\\\",\\n  \\\"long\\\": \\\"Attach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\\\\n\\\\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\\\\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\\\\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\\\\n\\\\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\\\\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\\\\n\\\\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\\\\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\\\\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\\\\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\\\\n\\\\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\\\\nexternal_agents in .entire/settings.local.json (that file only, and only\\\\nwhen it is untracked). Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\\\\n\\\\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\\\\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\\\",\\n  \\\"repo\\\": \\\"gh/entireio/entire-brain\\\",\\n  \\\"flags\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"agent\\\",\\n      \\\"shorthand\\\": \\\"a\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"claude-code\\\",\\n      \\\"usage\\\": \\\"Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external)\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"force\\\",\\n      \\\"shorthand\\\": \\\"f\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"bool\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"false\\\",\\n      \\\"usage\\\": \\\"Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"review\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"bool\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"false\\\",\\n      \\\"usage\\\": \\\"Tag the attached session as an agent review\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"skills\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"stringSlice\\\",\\n      \\\"default\\\": \\\"[]\\\",\\n      \\\"usage\\\": \\\"Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"context\\\",\\n      \\\"type\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n      \\\"usage\\\": \\\"Act as this saved login `name` for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\nCreate a trail for the current, a new, or no branch\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire trail create [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --add-assignee strings   Assign user(s) by login\\n      --base string            Base branch (defaults to detected default branch)\\n      --body string            Trail body\\n      --branch string          Branch for the trail (defaults to current branch)\\n      --checkout               Check out the branch after creating it\\n  -h, --help                   help for create\\n      --no-branch              Create a branchless trail\\n      --priority string        Priority (urgent, high, medium, low, none)\\n      --status string          Initial status (defaults to open)\\n      --title string           Trail title\\n      --type string            Type (bug, feature, task)\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n      --repo string    Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; defaults to the origin remote\\n{\\\"enabled\\\":true,\\\"agents\\\":[\\\"Claude Code\\\",\\\"Codex\\\",\\\"Pi\\\"],\\\"active_sessions\\\":[{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"Codex\\\",\\\"model\\\":\\\"gpt-6-astra\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"active\\\"}],\\\"agent_help\\\":\\\"entire agent-help\\\",\\\"hooks_outdated\\\":[\\\"claude-code\\\"],\\\"codex_hooks\\\":{\\\"state\\\":\\\"worktree_path_not_discovered\\\",\\\"worktree_path\\\":\\\"/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain/.codex/hooks.json\\\",\\\"discovered_path\\\":\\\"/Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain/.codex/hooks.json\\\",\\\"project_layer_path\\\":\\\"/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain/.codex\\\"},\\\"checkpoint_sync_remote\\\":\\\"origin\\\",\\\"checkpoint_sync_remote_source\\\":\\\"default\\\"}\\nExplain provides human-readable context about sessions, commits, and checkpoints.\\n\\nUse this command to understand what happened during agent-driven development,\\neither for self-review or to understand a teammate's work.\\n\\nBy default, shows checkpoints on the current branch. Pass a checkpoint ID or\\ncommit SHA as a positional argument to explain a specific item, or use flags.\\n\\nViewing specific items:\\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha>           Auto-detects checkpoint ID or commit SHA\\n  entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id>     Force interpretation as checkpoint ID\\n  entire checkpoint explain --commit <ref>        Force interpretation as commit ref\\n\\nCheckpoints in another repo:\\n  entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name\\n                 Explain a checkpoint owned by another repository — the\\n                 drill-down for a cross-repo 'entire search' hit. Reads it from\\n                 that repo's Entire API; nothing is written to this repo.\\n                 Needs a full checkpoint ID (positional or --checkpoint) and a\\n                 checkpoint that has been pushed.\\n\\nFiltering the list view:\\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\\n\\nOutput verbosity levels (when explaining a specific item):\\n  Default:         Detailed view with scoped prompts (ID, session, tokens, intent, prompts, files)\\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\\n\\nMachine-readable export modes (additive surface for external consumers):\\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given;\\n                   emits a single checkpoint envelope when a target is supplied.\\n                   Transcript bytes are NEVER embedded in the JSON envelope.\\n  --transcript     Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes (JSONL) to stdout\\n                   for the selected session. Same bytes as --raw-transcript\\n                   while checkpoints v1 is the checkpoint store.\\n  --session-index  Pick a session within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based).\\n                   Defaults to the latest session. Only meaningful with\\n                   --transcript or --raw-transcript.\\n  --limit          Cap the number of checkpoints returned by the list view.\\n                   Defaults to 100. When the cap is hit, a stderr note\\n                   says how many were skipped. Only meaningful with --json.\\n\\nSummary generation:\\n  --generate    Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\\n  --force       Regenerate even if a summary already exists (requires --generate)\\n\\nPerformance options:\\n  --search-all  Remove branch/depth limits when searching for commits (may be slow)\\n\\nCheckpoint detail view shows:\\n  - Author of the checkpoint\\n  - Associated git commits that reference the checkpoint\\n  - Prompts and responses from the session\\n\\nNote: --session filters the list view; the positional arg, --commit, and --checkpoint are mutually exclusive.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire checkpoint explain [checkpoint-id | commit-sha] [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -c, --checkpoint string             Explain a specific checkpoint (ID or prefix)\\n      --commit string                 Explain a specific commit (SHA or ref, \\\"commit-ish\\\")\\n      --force                         Regenerate summary even if one already exists (requires --generate)\\n      --full                          Show full parsed transcript (all prompts/responses)\\n      --generate                      Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\\n  -h, --help                          help for explain\\n      --insecure-http-auth            Allow plain-HTTP auth for --repo (local dev only)\\n      --json                          Output metadata as JSON (no transcript bytes)\\n      --limit int                     Cap the list view at N checkpoints (default: 100). Only meaningful with --json.\\n      --no-pager                      Disable pager output\\n      --raw-transcript                Show raw transcript file (JSONL format)\\n      --repo string                   Explain a checkpoint owned by another repo (owner/name or gh/owner/name), read from that repo's Entire API\\n      --search-all                    Search all commits (no branch/depth limit, may be slow)\\n      --session string                Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\\n      --session-index int             Session index within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based, defaults to latest) (default -1)\\n  -s, --short                         Show summary only (omit prompts and files)\\n      --summary-timeout-seconds int   Hard deadline in seconds for --generate summary generation; overrides summary_timeout_seconds setting. 0 = use setting; if setting is also unset or 0, no automatic deadline applies.\\n      --transcript                    Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes to stdout\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"0e5d1a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002791,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":418,\"output\":\"CODEX_THREAD_ID 01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9\\nrollout-2026-09-19T01-16-46-01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9.jsonl {'id': '01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9', 'cwd': '/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain', 'source': 'vscode', 'agent_role': None, 'parent_thread_id': None}\\nrollout-2026-09-19T21-59-47-01a0bb40-e543-7753-9bbb-8a6b1bbe67c8.jsonl {'id': '01a0bb40-e543-7753-9bbb-8a6b1bbe67c8', 'cwd': '/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain', 'source': {'subagent': {'thread_spawn': {'parent_thread_id': '01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9', 'depth': 1, 'agent_path': '/root/fix_f80', 'agent_nickname': 'Nash', 'agent_role': 'worker'}}}, 'agent_role': 'worker', 'parent_thread_id': '01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9'}\\nrollout-2026-09-19T22-00-14-01a0bb41-4d13-7682-87d7-7d0813beedea.jsonl {'id': '01a0bb41-4d13-7682-87d7-7d0813beedea', 'cwd': '/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain', 'source': {'subagent': {'thread_spawn': {'parent_thread_id': '01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9', 'depth': 1, 'agent_path': '/root/fix_f76', 'agent_nickname': 'Jason', 'agent_role': 'worker'}}}, 'agent_role': 'worker', 'parent_thread_id': '01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9'}\\nrollout-2026-09-19T22-00-01-01a0bb41-1adb-72e2-822f-4b8ee73f9e91.jsonl {'id': '01a0bb41-1adb-72e2-822f-4b8ee73f9e91', 'cwd': '/Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain', 'source': {'subagent': {'thread_spawn': {'parent_thread_id': '01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9', 'depth': 1, 'agent_path': '/root/fix_f58', 'agent_nickname': 'Goodall', 'agent_role': 'worker'}}}, 'agent_role': 'worker', 'parent_thread_id': '01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb