{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T20:06:14.297Z","ordinal":8603,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9","turn_id":"01a0bb40-0204-7de1-a470-e55eab47a99a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-da927446-5c89-4590-9763-5cd702417de4","process_id":"43554","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","entire brain search --help"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire brain search --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Lexical keyword search across facts, history, and docs (BM25 for history and docs; token-overlap for facts)\n\nUsage:\n  entire-brain search <query> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --after string          Conversation source only: sessions at or after this time (RFC3339 or YYYY-MM-DD)\n      --agent string          Conversation source only: exchanges captured by this agent/harness (e.g. \"Claude Code\", \"Codex\")\n      --before string         Conversation source only: sessions before this time (RFC3339 or YYYY-MM-DD)\n      --branch string         Branch for facts (default: current); with --source conversation also filters exchanges to that captured branch\n      --concept stringArray   Conversation source only: additional concept (repeatable, up to 4); sessions must match the query AND every concept\n      --format string         Output format: json or cli (QMD-style alias for --json)\n  -h, --help                  help for search\n      --include-abstract      Conversation source only: include bounded evidence-linked session previews (never affects ranking)\n      --json                  Emit machine-readable JSON\n      --limit int             Maximum results (default 10)\n  -n, --number int            Maximum results (QMD-style alias for --limit) (default 10)\n      --patterns              Also surface relevant pattern:/theme: pointers (does not change facts/history/docs ranking)\n      --session string        Conversation source only: exchanges from this session id (also disables the per-session diversity cap)\n      --source string         Restrict retrieval to one source: all, fact, history, conversation, or doc (default all; conversation is experimental opt-in)\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Lexical keyword search across facts, history, and docs (BM25 for history and docs; token-overlap for facts)\n\nUsage:\n  entire-brain search <query> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --after string          Conversation source only: sessions at or after this time (RFC3339 or YYYY-MM-DD)\n      --agent string          Conversation source only: exchanges captured by this agent/harness (e.g. \"Claude Code\", \"Codex\")\n      --before string         Conversation source only: sessions before this time (RFC3339 or YYYY-MM-DD)\n      --branch string         Branch for facts (default: current); with --source conversation also filters exchanges to that captured branch\n      --concept stringArray   Conversation source only: additional concept (repeatable, up to 4); sessions must match the query AND every concept\n      --format string         Output format: json or cli (QMD-style alias for --json)\n  -h, --help                  help for search\n      --include-abstract      Conversation source only: include bounded evidence-linked session previews (never affects ranking)\n      --json                  Emit machine-readable JSON\n      --limit int             Maximum results (default 10)\n  -n, --number int            Maximum results (QMD-style alias for --limit) (default 10)\n      --patterns              Also surface relevant pattern:/theme: pointers (does not change facts/history/docs ranking)\n      --session string        Conversation source only: exchanges from this session id (also disables the per-session diversity cap)\n      --source string         Restrict retrieval to one source: all, fact, history, conversation, or doc (default all; conversation is experimental opt-in)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3792},"formatted_output":"Lexical keyword search across facts, history, and docs (BM25 for history and docs; token-overlap for facts)\n\nUsage:\n  entire-brain search <query> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --after string          Conversation source only: sessions at or after this time (RFC3339 or YYYY-MM-DD)\n      --agent string          Conversation source only: exchanges captured by this agent/harness (e.g. \"Claude Code\", \"Codex\")\n      --before string         Conversation source only: sessions before this time (RFC3339 or YYYY-MM-DD)\n      --branch string         Branch for facts (default: current); with --source conversation also filters exchanges to that captured branch\n      --concept stringArray   Conversation source only: additional concept (repeatable, up to 4); sessions must match the query AND every concept\n      --format string         Output format: json or cli (QMD-style alias for --json)\n  -h, --help                  help for search\n      --include-abstract      Conversation source only: include bounded evidence-linked session previews (never affects ranking)\n      --json                  Emit machine-readable JSON\n      --limit int             Maximum results (default 10)\n  -n, --number int            Maximum results (QMD-style alias for --limit) (default 10)\n      --patterns              Also surface relevant pattern:/theme: pointers (does not change facts/history/docs ranking)\n      --session string        Conversation source only: exchanges from this session id (also disables the per-session diversity cap)\n      --source string         Restrict retrieval to one source: all, fact, history, conversation, or doc (default all; conversation is experimental opt-in)\n"},"started_at_ms":1789848374297,"completed_at_ms":1789848374297}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T20:06:14.440Z","ordinal":8604,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9","turn_id":"01a0bb40-0204-7de1-a470-e55eab47a99a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-93d6dde6-9a22-462f-b04d-f8e8981a4086","process_id":"45055","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","entire graph diff --help"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire graph diff --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Entity-level change list between two refs\n\nUsage:\n  entire graph diff --base <rev> --head <rev> [--json] [--progress] [--max-seconds n] [--repo path] [-- path...]\n\nEntity-level change list between two refs, with heuristic dependent counts. High dependent counts on a signature change mean run tests first. `analyze` is an alias for this command. Stops cleanly after --max-seconds and emits the partial result with W_ANALYSIS_BUDGET_EXCEEDED warnings.\n\nFlags:\n  --base <rev>        Base revision (default: HEAD~1)\n  --head <rev>        Head revision (default: HEAD)\n  --json              Emit the result as JSON\n  --progress          Emit progress events to stderr\n  --max-seconds <n>   Analysis budget; 0 = unlimited (default: 120)\n  --repo <path>       Repository (default: current repo)\n\nExamples:\n  entire graph diff --base main --head HEAD --json\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Entity-level change list between two refs\n\nUsage:\n  entire graph diff --base <rev> --head <rev> [--json] [--progress] [--max-seconds n] [--repo path] [-- path...]\n\nEntity-level change list between two refs, with heuristic dependent counts. High dependent counts on a signature change mean run tests first. `analyze` is an alias for this command. Stops cleanly after --max-seconds and emits the partial result with W_ANALYSIS_BUDGET_EXCEEDED warnings.\n\nFlags:\n  --base <rev>        Base revision (default: HEAD~1)\n  --head <rev>        Head revision (default: HEAD)\n  --json              Emit the result as JSON\n  --progress          Emit progress events to stderr\n  --max-seconds <n>   Analysis budget; 0 = unlimited (default: 120)\n  --repo <path>       Repository (default: current repo)\n\nExamples:\n  entire graph diff --base main --head HEAD --json\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3250},"formatted_output":"Entity-level change list between two refs\n\nUsage:\n  entire graph diff --base <rev> --head <rev> [--json] [--progress] [--max-seconds n] [--repo path] [-- path...]\n\nEntity-level change list between two refs, with heuristic dependent counts. High dependent counts on a signature change mean run tests first. `analyze` is an alias for this command. Stops cleanly after --max-seconds and emits the partial result with W_ANALYSIS_BUDGET_EXCEEDED warnings.\n\nFlags:\n  --base <rev>        Base revision (default: HEAD~1)\n  --head <rev>        Head revision (default: HEAD)\n  --json              Emit the result as JSON\n  --progress          Emit progress events to stderr\n  --max-seconds <n>   Analysis budget; 0 = unlimited (default: 120)\n  --repo <path>       Repository (default: current repo)\n\nExamples:\n  entire graph diff --base main --head HEAD --json\n"},"started_at_ms":1789848374440,"completed_at_ms":1789848374440}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T20:06:14.576Z","ordinal":8605,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9","turn_id":"01a0bb40-0204-7de1-a470-e55eab47a99a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3a2ce54b-1925-4ac0-8be3-e20bcc29a566","process_id":"76187","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","entire session attach --help"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire session attach --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Attach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\n\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\n\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\n\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\n\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\nexternal_agents in .entire/settings.local.json (that file only, and only\nwhen it is untracked). Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\n\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\n\nUsage:\n  entire session attach <session-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -a, --agent string     Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external) (default \"claude-code\")\n  -f, --force            Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\n  -h, --help             help for attach\n      --review           Tag the attached session as an agent review\n      --skills strings   Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Attach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\n\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\n\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\n\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\n\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\nexternal_agents in .entire/settings.local.json (that file only, and only\nwhen it is untracked). Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\n\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\n\nUsage:\n  entire session attach <session-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -a, --agent string     Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external) (default \"claude-code\")\n  -f, --force            Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\n  -h, --help             help for attach\n      --review           Tag the attached session as an agent review\n      --skills strings   Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":3333},"formatted_output":"Attach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\n\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\n\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\n\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\n\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\nexternal_agents in .entire/settings.local.json (that file only, and only\nwhen it is untracked). Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\n\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\n\nUsage:\n  entire session attach <session-id> [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -a, --agent string     Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external) (default \"claude-code\")\n  -f, --force            Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\n  -h, --help             help for attach\n      --review           Tag the attached session as an agent review\n      --skills strings   Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n"},"started_at_ms":1789848374576,"completed_at_ms":1789848374576}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T20:06:14.633Z","ordinal":8606,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0bb46-cd69-7a80-b09b-1b1e411da342","call_id":"call_vZ18znZzdTtjJ2U7Okefx3TA","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"508966\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003792,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":418,\"output\":\"Lexical keyword search across facts, history, and docs (BM25 for history and docs; token-overlap for facts)\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire-brain search <query> [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n      --after string          Conversation source only: sessions at or after this time (RFC3339 or YYYY-MM-DD)\\n      --agent string          Conversation source only: exchanges captured by this agent/harness (e.g. \\\"Claude Code\\\", \\\"Codex\\\")\\n      --before string         Conversation source only: sessions before this time (RFC3339 or YYYY-MM-DD)\\n      --branch string         Branch for facts (default: current); with --source conversation also filters exchanges to that captured branch\\n      --concept stringArray   Conversation source only: additional concept (repeatable, up to 4); sessions must match the query AND every concept\\n      --format string         Output format: json or cli (QMD-style alias for --json)\\n  -h, --help                  help for search\\n      --include-abstract      Conversation source only: include bounded evidence-linked session previews (never affects ranking)\\n      --json                  Emit machine-readable JSON\\n      --limit int             Maximum results (default 10)\\n  -n, --number int            Maximum results (QMD-style alias for --limit) (default 10)\\n      --patterns              Also surface relevant pattern:/theme: pointers (does not change facts/history/docs ranking)\\n      --session string        Conversation source only: exchanges from this session id (also disables the per-session diversity cap)\\n      --source string         Restrict retrieval to one source: all, fact, history, conversation, or doc (default all; conversation is experimental opt-in)\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"798a7a\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.00000325,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":213,\"output\":\"Entity-level change list between two refs\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire graph diff --base <rev> --head <rev> [--json] [--progress] [--max-seconds n] [--repo path] [-- path...]\\n\\nEntity-level change list between two refs, with heuristic dependent counts. High dependent counts on a signature change mean run tests first. `analyze` is an alias for this command. Stops cleanly after --max-seconds and emits the partial result with W_ANALYSIS_BUDGET_EXCEEDED warnings.\\n\\nFlags:\\n  --base <rev>        Base revision (default: HEAD~1)\\n  --head <rev>        Head revision (default: HEAD)\\n  --json              Emit the result as JSON\\n  --progress          Emit progress events to stderr\\n  --max-seconds <n>   Analysis budget; 0 = unlimited (default: 120)\\n  --repo <path>       Repository (default: current repo)\\n\\nExamples:\\n  entire graph diff --base main --head HEAD --json\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"4c1b67\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000003333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":442,\"output\":\"Attach an existing agent session that wasn't captured by hooks.\\n\\nThis creates a checkpoint from the session's transcript and links it to the\\nlast commit. Use this when hooks failed to fire or weren't installed when\\nthe session started, or to attach a research session.\\n\\nIf the last commit already has a checkpoint, the session is added to it.\\nOtherwise a new checkpoint is created.\\n\\nUse --review to tag the attached session as an agent review. The\\nfirst user prompt in the transcript is recorded as the review prompt.\\nPass --skills to declare which skills were actually run; omit to\\nattach a review without a declared skills list.\\n\\nWorks with any registered agent, including external agents enabled via\\nexternal_agents in .entire/settings.local.json (that file only, and only\\nwhen it is untracked). Run 'entire agent list' to see the full list.\\n\\nIf --agent doesn't locate a transcript, Entire auto-detects the agent from\\nthe transcript and prints the detected agent name.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  entire session attach <session-id> [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -a, --agent string     Agent that created the session (see 'entire agent list' for registered agents, including external) (default \\\"claude-code\\\")\\n  -f, --force            Skip confirmation and amend the last commit with the checkpoint trailer (best-effort; if the amend fails the checkpoint is still created and the trailer is printed for manual paste)\\n  -h, --help             help for attach\\n      --review           Tag the attached session as an agent review\\n      --skills strings   Optional: declare which review skills were run in this session. Only used with --review\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0bb40-0204-7de1-a470-e55eab47a99a","create_time":1789848374.633563}}}
