he trail (defaults to current branch)\n      --checkout               Check out the branch after creating it\n  -h, --help                   help for create\n      --no-branch              Create a branchless trail\n      --priority string        Priority (urgent, high, medium, low, none)\n      --status string          Initial status (defaults to open)\n      --title string           Trail title\n      --type string            Type (bug, feature, task)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --repo string    Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; defaults to the origin remote\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":2875},"formatted_output":"Create a trail for the current, a new, or no branch\n\nUsage:\n  entire trail create [flags]\n\nFlags:\n      --add-assignee strings   Assign user(s) by login\n      --base string            Base branch (defaults to detected default branch)\n      --body string            Trail body\n      --branch string          Branch for the trail (defaults to current branch)\n      --checkout               Check out the branch after creating it\n  -h, --help                   help for create\n      --no-branch              Create a branchless trail\n      --priority string        Priority (urgent, high, medium, low, none)\n      --status string          Initial status (defaults to open)\n      --title string           Trail title\n      --type string            Type (bug, feature, task)\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n      --repo string    Target repository as forge/owner/repo (e.g. gh/acme/app) or a clone URL; defaults to the origin remote\n"},"started_at_ms":1789848389794,"completed_at_ms":1789848389794}}
{"timestamp":"2026-09-19T20:06:29.951Z","ordinal":8626,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0b6ce-e2ad-7853-bb2f-19731062a2c9","turn_id":"01a0bb40-0204-7de1-a470-e55eab47a99a","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ab735261-04ef-4272-ba07-eb1f0b5a585d","process_id":"78315","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","entire checkpoint explain --help"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/.codex/worktrees/5d33/entire-brain","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"entire checkpoint explain --help"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"Explain provides human-readable context about sessions, commits, and checkpoints.\n\nUse this command to understand what happened during agent-driven development,\neither for self-review or to understand a teammate's work.\n\nBy default, shows checkpoints on the current branch. Pass a checkpoint ID or\ncommit SHA as a positional argument to explain a specific item, or use flags.\n\nViewing specific items:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha>           Auto-detects checkpoint ID or commit SHA\n  entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id>     Force interpretation as checkpoint ID\n  entire checkpoint explain --commit <ref>        Force interpretation as commit ref\n\nCheckpoints in another repo:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name\n                 Explain a checkpoint owned by another repository — the\n                 drill-down for a cross-repo 'entire search' hit. Reads it from\n                 that repo's Entire API; nothing is written to this repo.\n                 Needs a full checkpoint ID (positional or --checkpoint) and a\n                 checkpoint that has been pushed.\n\nFiltering the list view:\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n\nOutput verbosity levels (when explaining a specific item):\n  Default:         Detailed view with scoped prompts (ID, session, tokens, intent, prompts, files)\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n\nMachine-readable export modes (additive surface for external consumers):\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given;\n                   emits a single checkpoint envelope when a target is supplied.\n                   Transcript bytes are NEVER embedded in the JSON envelope.\n  --transcript     Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes (JSONL) to stdout\n                   for the selected session. Same bytes as --raw-transcript\n                   while checkpoints v1 is the checkpoint store.\n  --session-index  Pick a session within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based).\n                   Defaults to the latest session. Only meaningful with\n                   --transcript or --raw-transcript.\n  --limit          Cap the number of checkpoints returned by the list view.\n                   Defaults to 100. When the cap is hit, a stderr note\n                   says how many were skipped. Only meaningful with --json.\n\nSummary generation:\n  --generate    Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\n  --force       Regenerate even if a summary already exists (requires --generate)\n\nPerformance options:\n  --search-all  Remove branch/depth limits when searching for commits (may be slow)\n\nCheckpoint detail view shows:\n  - Author of the checkpoint\n  - Associated git commits that reference the checkpoint\n  - Prompts and responses from the session\n\nNote: --session filters the list view; the positional arg, --commit, and --checkpoint are mutually exclusive.\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint explain [checkpoint-id | commit-sha] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -c, --checkpoint string             Explain a specific checkpoint (ID or prefix)\n      --commit string                 Explain a specific commit (SHA or ref, \"commit-ish\")\n      --force                         Regenerate summary even if one already exists (requires --generate)\n      --full                          Show full parsed transcript (all prompts/responses)\n      --generate                      Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\n  -h, --help                          help for explain\n      --insecure-http-auth            Allow plain-HTTP auth for --repo (local dev only)\n      --json                          Output metadata as JSON (no transcript bytes)\n      --limit int                     Cap the list view at N checkpoints (default: 100). Only meaningful with --json.\n      --no-pager                      Disable pager output\n      --raw-transcript                Show raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n      --repo string                   Explain a checkpoint owned by another repo (owner/name or gh/owner/name), read from that repo's Entire API\n      --search-all                    Search all commits (no branch/depth limit, may be slow)\n      --session string                Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n      --session-index int             Session index within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based, defaults to latest) (default -1)\n  -s, --short                         Show summary only (omit prompts and files)\n      --summary-timeout-seconds int   Hard deadline in seconds for --generate summary generation; overrides summary_timeout_seconds setting. 0 = use setting; if setting is also unset or 0, no automatic deadline applies.\n      --transcript                    Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes to stdout\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"Explain provides human-readable context about sessions, commits, and checkpoints.\n\nUse this command to understand what happened during agent-driven development,\neither for self-review or to understand a teammate's work.\n\nBy default, shows checkpoints on the current branch. Pass a checkpoint ID or\ncommit SHA as a positional argument to explain a specific item, or use flags.\n\nViewing specific items:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha>           Auto-detects checkpoint ID or commit SHA\n  entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id>     Force interpretation as checkpoint ID\n  entire checkpoint explain --commit <ref>        Force interpretation as commit ref\n\nCheckpoints in another repo:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name\n                 Explain a checkpoint owned by another repository — the\n                 drill-down for a cross-repo 'entire search' hit. Reads it from\n                 that repo's Entire API; nothing is written to this repo.\n                 Needs a full checkpoint ID (positional or --checkpoint) and a\n                 checkpoint that has been pushed.\n\nFiltering the list view:\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n\nOutput verbosity levels (when explaining a specific item):\n  Default:         Detailed view with scoped prompts (ID, session, tokens, intent, prompts, files)\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n\nMachine-readable export modes (additive surface for external consumers):\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given;\n                   emits a single checkpoint envelope when a target is supplied.\n                   Transcript bytes are NEVER embedded in the JSON envelope.\n  --transcript     Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes (JSONL) to stdout\n                   for the selected session. Same bytes as --raw-transcript\n                   while checkpoints v1 is the checkpoint store.\n  --session-index  Pick a session within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based).\n                   Defaults to the latest session. Only meaningful with\n                   --transcript or --raw-transcript.\n  --limit          Cap the number of checkpoints returned by the list view.\n                   Defaults to 100. When the cap is hit, a stderr note\n                   says how many were skipped. Only meaningful with --json.\n\nSummary generation:\n  --generate    Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\n  --force       Regenerate even if a summary already exists (requires --generate)\n\nPerformance options:\n  --search-all  Remove branch/depth limits when searching for commits (may be slow)\n\nCheckpoint detail view shows:\n  - Author of the checkpoint\n  - Associated git commits that reference the checkpoint\n  - Prompts and responses from the session\n\nNote: --session filters the list view; the positional arg, --commit, and --checkpoint are mutually exclusive.\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint explain [checkpoint-id | commit-sha] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -c, --checkpoint string             Explain a specific checkpoint (ID or prefix)\n      --commit string                 Explain a specific commit (SHA or ref, \"commit-ish\")\n      --force                         Regenerate summary even if one already exists (requires --generate)\n      --full                          Show full parsed transcript (all prompts/responses)\n      --generate                      Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\n  -h, --help                          help for explain\n      --insecure-http-auth            Allow plain-HTTP auth for --repo (local dev only)\n      --json                          Output metadata as JSON (no transcript bytes)\n      --limit int                     Cap the list view at N checkpoints (default: 100). Only meaningful with --json.\n      --no-pager                      Disable pager output\n      --raw-transcript                Show raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n      --repo string                   Explain a checkpoint owned by another repo (owner/name or gh/owner/name), read from that repo's Entire API\n      --search-all                    Search all commits (no branch/depth limit, may be slow)\n      --session string                Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n      --session-index int             Session index within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based, defaults to latest) (default -1)\n  -s, --short                         Show summary only (omit prompts and files)\n      --summary-timeout-seconds int   Hard deadline in seconds for --generate summary generation; overrides summary_timeout_seconds setting. 0 = use setting; if setting is also unset or 0, no automatic deadline applies.\n      --transcript                    Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes to stdout\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":4334},"formatted_output":"Explain provides human-readable context about sessions, commits, and checkpoints.\n\nUse this command to understand what happened during agent-driven development,\neither for self-review or to understand a teammate's work.\n\nBy default, shows checkpoints on the current branch. Pass a checkpoint ID or\ncommit SHA as a positional argument to explain a specific item, or use flags.\n\nViewing specific items:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id-or-sha>           Auto-detects checkpoint ID or commit SHA\n  entire checkpoint explain --checkpoint <id>     Force interpretation as checkpoint ID\n  entire checkpoint explain --commit <ref>        Force interpretation as commit ref\n\nCheckpoints in another repo:\n  entire checkpoint explain <id> --repo owner/name\n                 Explain a checkpoint owned by another repository — the\n                 drill-down for a cross-repo 'entire search' hit. Reads it from\n                 that repo's Entire API; nothing is written to this repo.\n                 Needs a full checkpoint ID (positional or --checkpoint) and a\n                 checkpoint that has been pushed.\n\nFiltering the list view:\n  --session      Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n\nOutput verbosity levels (when explaining a specific item):\n  Default:         Detailed view with scoped prompts (ID, session, tokens, intent, prompts, files)\n  --short          Summary only (ID, session, timestamp, tokens, intent)\n  --full           Parsed full transcript (all prompts/responses from entire session)\n  --raw-transcript Raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n\nMachine-readable export modes (additive surface for external consumers):\n  --json           Metadata-only JSON. Lists checkpoints when no target is given;\n                   emits a single checkpoint envelope when a target is supplied.\n                   Transcript bytes are NEVER embedded in the JSON envelope.\n  --transcript     Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes (JSONL) to stdout\n                   for the selected session. Same bytes as --raw-transcript\n                   while checkpoints v1 is the checkpoint store.\n  --session-index  Pick a session within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based).\n                   Defaults to the latest session. Only meaningful with\n                   --transcript or --raw-transcript.\n  --limit          Cap the number of checkpoints returned by the list view.\n                   Defaults to 100. When the cap is hit, a stderr note\n                   says how many were skipped. Only meaningful with --json.\n\nSummary generation:\n  --generate    Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\n  --force       Regenerate even if a summary already exists (requires --generate)\n\nPerformance options:\n  --search-all  Remove branch/depth limits when searching for commits (may be slow)\n\nCheckpoint detail view shows:\n  - Author of the checkpoint\n  - Associated git commits that reference the checkpoint\n  - Prompts and responses from the session\n\nNote: --session filters the list view; the positional arg, --commit, and --checkpoint are mutually exclusive.\n\nUsage:\n  entire checkpoint explain [checkpoint-id | commit-sha] [flags]\n\nFlags:\n  -c, --checkpoint string             Explain a specific checkpoint (ID or prefix)\n      --commit string                 Explain a specific commit (SHA or ref, \"commit-ish\")\n      --force                         Regenerate summary even if one already exists (requires --generate)\n      --full                          Show full parsed transcript (all prompts/responses)\n      --generate                      Generate an AI summary for the checkpoint\n  -h, --help                          help for explain\n      --insecure-http-auth            Allow plain-HTTP auth for --repo (local dev only)\n      --json                          Output metadata as JSON (no transcript bytes)\n      --limit int                     Cap the list view at N checkpoints (default: 100). Only meaningful with --json.\n      --no-pager                      Disable pager output\n      --raw-transcript                Show raw transcript file (JSONL format)\n      --repo string                   Explain a checkpoint owned by another repo (owner/name or gh/owner/name), read from that repo's Entire API\n      --search-all                    Search all commits (no branch/depth limit, may be slow)\n      --session string                Filter checkpoints by session ID (or prefix)\n      --session-index int             Session index within a multi-session checkpoint (0-based, defaults to latest) (default -1)\n  -s, --short                         Show summary only (omit prompts and files)\n      --summary-timeout-seconds int   Hard deadline in seconds for --generate summary generation; overrides summary_timeout_seconds setting. 0 = use setting; if setting is also unset or 0, no automatic deadline applies.\n      --transcript                    Stream stored checkpoint transcript bytes to stdout\n\nGlobal Flags:\n      --context name   Act as this saved login name for this command only, instead of the active context (entire auth contexts lists them)\n"},"started_at_ms":1789848389951,"completed_at_ms":1789848389951}}
